window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 05 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000070381","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"In the word \"TECHNOLOGY\", what is the difference in index (A=1 to Z=26) between the 3<sup>rd</sup> and 7<sup>th</sup> letters? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शब्द \"TECHNOLOGY\" में तीसरे और सातवें अक्षर के सूचकांक (A=1 से Z=26) में क्या अंतर है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"5"},"3":{"en":"7"},"4":{"en":"9"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Counting the letters of TECHNOLOGY: T, E, C, H, N, O, L, O, G, Y<br>The 3rd letter is C, whose index is 3, and the 7th letter is L, whose index is 12<br>So the difference is 12 − 3 = 9<br>Hence the difference in index is 9<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 9.</b>","hi":"TECHNOLOGY के अक्षर गिनने पर: T, E, C, H, N, O, L, O, G, Y<br>तीसरा अक्षर C है, जिसका सूचकांक 3 है, तथा सातवाँ अक्षर L है, जिसका सूचकांक 12 है<br>अतः अंतर 12 − 3 = 9 है<br>इसलिए सूचकांक में अंतर 9 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000070382","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A number, when divided by 5 or 10, leaves a remainder of 3. What will be the remainder when the square of that number is divided by 5? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कोई संख्या 5 या 10 से भाग देने पर शेषफल 3 देती है। उस संख्या का वर्ग 5 से भाग देने पर शेषफल क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A number that leaves the remainder 3 when divided by 10 can be written as 10k + 3, which is also of the form 5m + 3<br>Squaring it, (5m + 3)² = 25m² + 30m + 9 = 5(5m² + 6m + 1) + 4<br>So the remainder on dividing by 5 is 4<br>Hence the remainder is 4<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4.</b>","hi":"जो संख्या 10 से भाग देने पर 3 शेष देती है, उसे 10k + 3 लिखा जा सकता है, जो 5m + 3 के रूप में भी है<br>उसका वर्ग (5m + 3)² = 25m² + 30m + 9 = 5(5m² + 6m + 1) + 4 है<br>अतः 5 से भाग देने पर शेषफल 4 है<br>इसलिए शेषफल 4 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000070383","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br>2, 6, 18, ___ [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रेणी में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br>2, 6, 18, ___ [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"56"},"2":{"en":"54"},"3":{"en":"52"},"4":{"en":"58"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Every term is three times the term before it: 2 × 3 = 6 and 6 × 3 = 18 ✔<br>So the next term is 18 × 3 = 54<br>Hence the next number is 54<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 54.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अपने पहले के पद का तीन गुना है: 2 × 3 = 6 तथा 6 × 3 = 18 ✔<br>अतः अगला पद 18 × 3 = 54 है<br>इसलिए अगली संख्या 54 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 54 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000070384","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What is the simple interest earned on an investment of &#8377;5,000 for a period of 3 years at an annual interest rate of 5%? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"5,000 रुपये के निवेश पर 5% वार्षिक ब्याज दर से 3 वर्षों में अर्जित साधारण ब्याज क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"&#8377;750","hi":"750 रुपये"},"2":{"en":"&#8377;800","hi":"800 रुपये"},"3":{"en":"&#8377;850","hi":"850 रुपये"},"4":{"en":"&#8377;900","hi":"900 रुपये"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Simple interest is P × R × T / 100<br>So the interest is 5000 × 5 × 3 / 100 = 750<br>Hence the simple interest earned is &#8377;750<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): &#8377;750.</b>","hi":"साधारण ब्याज = P × R × T / 100<br>अतः ब्याज 5000 × 5 × 3 / 100 = 750 है<br>इसलिए अर्जित साधारण ब्याज 750 रुपये है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 750 रुपये है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000070385","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"<b>Instruction:</b> Choose the inference that is clearly supported by the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b> All applicants accepted into the highly competitive Master's program scored in the top 5% on the entrance examination, and submitted a strong letter of recommendation from a university professor.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>Inference I: An applicant who did not score in the top 5% on the entrance examination was not accepted into the Master's program.<br>Inference II: A strong letter of recommendation from a university professor is the sole factor determining acceptance into the Master's program. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निर्देश: वह निष्कर्ष चुनिए जो कथन से स्पष्ट रूप से समर्थित है।<br>कथन: अत्यधिक प्रतिस्पर्धी मास्टर कार्यक्रम में स्वीकृत सभी अभ्यर्थियों ने प्रवेश परीक्षा में शीर्ष 5% में स्थान प्राप्त किया था और किसी विश्वविद्यालय के प्रोफेसर से एक मजबूत अनुशंसा पत्र प्रस्तुत किया था।<br>निष्कर्ष:<br>निष्कर्ष I: जिस अभ्यर्थी ने प्रवेश परीक्षा में शीर्ष 5% में स्थान नहीं प्राप्त किया, उसे मास्टर कार्यक्रम में स्वीकृति नहीं मिली।<br>निष्कर्ष II: विश्वविद्यालय के प्रोफेसर से मजबूत अनुशंसा पत्र ही मास्टर कार्यक्रम में स्वीकृति का एकमात्र निर्धारक है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Every accepted applicant was in the top 5%, so anyone who was not in the top 5% cannot be among the accepted applicants, and inference I follows ✔<br>The statement gives two conditions, so a strong letter of recommendation is necessary but is not shown to be the only factor, and inference II is too strong ✘<br>Hence only inference I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Inference I follows.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक स्वीकृत अभ्यर्थी शीर्ष 5% में था, अतः जो शीर्ष 5% में नहीं है वह स्वीकृत अभ्यर्थियों में नहीं हो सकता, और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>कथन दो शर्तें देता है, अतः मजबूत अनुशंसा पत्र आवश्यक है परंतु एकमात्र कारक सिद्ध नहीं होता, और निष्कर्ष II अत्यधिक है ✘<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000070386","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If DOCTOR is coded as EPDUPS, how is EPDUPS coded? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि DOCTOR का कूट EPDUPS है, तो EPDUPS का कूट क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"FQEVQT"},"2":{"en":"FQFVRU"},"3":{"en":"FQEVRT"},"4":{"en":"FQEVQU"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In DOCTOR every letter moves one place ahead: D→E, O→P, C→D, T→U, O→P and R→S, which gives EPDUPS ✔<br>Applying the same step to EPDUPS: E→F, P→Q, D→E, U→V, P→Q and S→T<br>Hence EPDUPS is coded as FQEVQT<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): FQEVQT.</b>","hi":"DOCTOR में प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे जाता है: D→E, O→P, C→D, T→U, O→P तथा R→S, जिससे EPDUPS मिलता है ✔<br>EPDUPS पर वही चरण लगाने से E→F, P→Q, D→E, U→V, P→Q तथा S→T<br>इसलिए EPDUPS का कूट FQEVQT है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): FQEVQT है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000070387","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Carefully examine the address below and identify which of the following alternatives matches the given address.<br>Ms. A. Mishra<br>8902 Crescent View, 10th Floor, Malviya Nagar<br>Delhi - 110017<br><b>Alternatives:</b><br>A) Ms. A. Mishra, 8902 Crescent View, 10th Floor, Malviya Nagar, Delhi - 110017<br>B) Ms. A. Mishra, 8902 Crescent View, 9th Floor, Malviya Nagar, Delhi - 110018<br>C) Ms. A. Mishra, 8902 Crescent View, 10th Floor, Malviya Nagar, Delhi - 110016<br>D) Ms. A. Mishra, 8902 Crescent View, 10th Floor, Malviya Nagar, Delhi - 110017 [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नीचे दिए पते को ध्यान से देखिए और पहचानिए कि निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प दिए गए पते से मेल खाता है।<br>Ms. A. Mishra<br>8902 Crescent View, 10th Floor, Malviya Nagar<br>Delhi - 110017<br><b>विकल्प:</b><br>A) Ms. A. Mishra, 8902 Crescent View, 10th Floor, Malviya Nagar, Delhi - 110017<br>B) Ms. A. Mishra, 8902 Crescent View, 9th Floor, Malviya Nagar, Delhi - 110018<br>C) Ms. A. Mishra, 8902 Crescent View, 10th Floor, Malviya Nagar, Delhi - 110016<br>D) Ms. A. Mishra, 8902 Crescent View, 10th Floor, Malviya Nagar, Delhi - 110017 [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D and B","hi":"D और B"},"2":{"en":"B and C","hi":"B और C"},"3":{"en":"A and D","hi":"A और D"},"4":{"en":"C and A","hi":"C और A"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The given address has the 10th Floor and the pin code 110017<br>Alternative B changes the floor to the 9th and the pin code to 110018, and alternative C changes the pin code to 110016<br>Alternatives A and D repeat every part of the address exactly<br>Hence A and D match the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): A and D.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते में 10वीं मंजिल तथा पिन कोड 110017 है<br>विकल्प B में मंजिल 9वीं और पिन कोड 110018 है, तथा विकल्प C में पिन कोड 110016 है<br>विकल्प A और D पते के प्रत्येक भाग को ठीक वैसा ही दोहराते हैं<br>इसलिए A और D दिए गए पते से मेल खाते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): A और D है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000070388","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"WORLD\" is written as \"DLROW.\" How will \"CHAIR\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"WORLD\" को \"DLROW\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"CHAIR\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"HIRAC"},"2":{"en":"AHRIC"},"3":{"en":"RIAHC"},"4":{"en":"RHAIC"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"WORLD written backwards reads D L R O W, which is exactly the code DLROW<br>So the letters of the word are simply reversed<br>CHAIR reversed reads R I A H C<br>Hence CHAIR is written as RIAHC<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): RIAHC.</b>","hi":"WORLD उल्टा लिखने पर D L R O W मिलता है, जो ठीक कूट DLROW है<br>अतः शब्द के अक्षरों को केवल उलट दिया जाता है<br>CHAIR उल्टा लिखने पर R I A H C मिलता है<br>इसलिए CHAIR को RIAHC लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): RIAHC है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000070389","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Two pipes can fill a tank in 16 hours and 24 hours, respectively, while a third pipe can empty it in 48 hours. If all three pipes are opened together, what fraction of the tank will be filled in 8 hours? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो पाइप एक टंकी को क्रमशः 16 घंटे तथा 24 घंटे में भर सकते हैं, जबकि तीसरा पाइप उसे 48 घंटे में खाली कर सकता है। यदि तीनों पाइप एक साथ खोल दिए जाएँ, तो 8 घंटे में टंकी का कितना भाग भर जाएगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2/3"},"2":{"en":"3/4"},"3":{"en":"5/6"},"4":{"en":"7/8"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In one hour the first pipe fills 1/16, the second 1/24 and the third empties 1/48 of the tank<br>The net filling in one hour is 1/16 + 1/24 − 1/48 = 3/48 + 2/48 − 1/48 = 4/48 = 1/12<br>In 8 hours the tank is filled to 8/12 = 2/3<br>Hence 2/3 of the tank is filled in 8 hours<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2/3.</b>","hi":"एक घंटे में पहला पाइप 1/16, दूसरा 1/24 भरता है तथा तीसरा 1/48 खाली करता है<br>एक घंटे में शुद्ध भराव 1/16 + 1/24 − 1/48 = 3/48 + 2/48 − 1/48 = 4/48 = 1/12 है<br>8 घंटे में टंकी 8/12 = 2/3 भर जाती है<br>इसलिए 8 घंटे में टंकी का 2/3 भाग भर जाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2/3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000070390","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.<br><b>Original Address:</b><br>Suite No 18B7Grand Royal Residency Tower 14Saint Patrick Avenue Sector 9Brooklyn New York NY 11217United States of America [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है।<br><b>मूल पता:</b><br>Suite No 18B7Grand Royal Residency Tower 14Saint Patrick Avenue Sector 9Brooklyn New York NY 11217United States of America [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Suite No 18B7Grand Royal Residency Tower 14Saint Patrick Avenue Sector 9Brooklyn NewYork NY 11217United States of America"},"2":{"en":"Suite No 18B7Grand Royal Residency Tower 14Saint Patrick Avenue Sector 9Brooklyn New York NY 12117United States of America"},"3":{"en":"Suite No 18B7Grand Royal Residency Tower 41Saint Patrick Avenue Sector 9Brooklyn New York NY 11217United States of America"},"4":{"en":"Suite No 18B7Grand Royal Residency Tower 14Saint Patrick Avenue Sector 9Brooklyn New York NY 11217United States of America"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The original address has Tower 14, New York and the zip code 11217<br>The first option writes NewYork without the space, the second changes the zip code to 12117 and the third changes the tower to 41<br>Only the fourth option repeats the original address exactly<br>Hence the fourth option perfectly matches the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Suite No 18B7Grand Royal Residency Tower 14Saint Patrick Avenue Sector 9Brooklyn New York NY 11217United States of America.</b>","hi":"मूल पते में Tower 14, New York तथा ज़िप कोड 11217 है<br>पहले विकल्प में NewYork बिना स्थान के है, दूसरे में ज़िप कोड 12117 है तथा तीसरे में टावर 41 है<br>केवल चौथा विकल्प मूल पते को ठीक वैसा ही दोहराता है<br>अतः चौथा विकल्प दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Suite No 18B7Grand Royal Residency Tower 14Saint Patrick Avenue Sector 9Brooklyn New York NY 11217United States of America है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000070391","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"<b>Directions:</b> Use the following definitions to answer the question that follows.<br>1. P # Q means P is the father of Q.<br>2. P &#36; Q means P is the sister of Q.<br>3. P * Q means P is the son of Q.<br>4. P ^ Q means P is the wife of Q.<br>5. P ! Q means P is the mother of Q.<br><b>Question:</b> If 'M ! N * O # P ^ Q', how is Q related to M? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>निर्देश:</b> आगे दिए प्रश्न का उत्तर देने के लिए निम्नलिखित परिभाषाओं का प्रयोग कीजिए।<br>1. P # Q का अर्थ है P, Q का पिता है।<br>2. P &#36; Q का अर्थ है P, Q की बहन है।<br>3. P * Q का अर्थ है P, Q का पुत्र है।<br>4. P ^ Q का अर्थ है P, Q की पत्नी है।<br>5. P ! Q का अर्थ है P, Q की माता है।<br><b>प्रश्न:</b> यदि 'M ! N * O # P ^ Q' है, तो Q, M से किस प्रकार संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Son-in-law","hi":"दामाद"},"2":{"en":"Son","hi":"पुत्र"},"3":{"en":"Brother","hi":"भाई"},"4":{"en":"Paternal Uncle","hi":"चाचा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"M ! N means M is the mother of N, and N * O means N is the son of O<br>O # P means O is the father of P, and P ^ Q means P is the wife of Q<br>So P is the daughter of O and M, and Q is the husband of P<br>Therefore Q is the son-in-law of M<br>Hence Q is related to M as son-in-law<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Son-in-law.</b>","hi":"M ! N का अर्थ है M, N की माता है, और N * O का अर्थ है N, O का पुत्र है<br>O # P का अर्थ है O, P का पिता है, और P ^ Q का अर्थ है P, Q की पत्नी है<br>अतः P, O और M की पुत्री है, तथा Q, P का पति है<br>इसलिए Q, M का दामाद है<br>अतः Q, M से दामाद के रूप में संबंधित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): दामाद है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000070392","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>HAB, DBX, ZCT, ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न जाँचिए और श्रेणी में अगला अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>HAB, DBX, ZCT, ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"VDP"},"2":{"en":"VCP"},"3":{"en":"VEQ"},"4":{"en":"VDR"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letters H, D, Z move four places back each time, so the next first letter is V<br>The second letters A, B, C move one place ahead each time, so the next second letter is D<br>The third letters B, X, T move four places back each time, so the next third letter is P<br>Hence the next set of letters is VDP<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): VDP.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर H, D, Z प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर V है<br>दूसरे अक्षर A, B, C प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर D है<br>तीसरे अक्षर B, X, T प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला तीसरा अक्षर P है<br>इसलिए अगला अक्षर-समूह VDP है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): VDP है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000070393","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following centre code does not follow the pattern of \"two consonants followed by the sum of their positions in the alphabet\"? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा केंद्र कूट \"दो व्यंजनों और उनके वर्णमाला स्थानों के योग\" के पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BD6"},"2":{"en":"CF9"},"3":{"en":"DH11"},"4":{"en":"GL19"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In BD6 the positions are B = 2 and D = 4, whose sum is 6 ✔<br>In CF9, C = 3 and F = 6 give 9 ✔, and in GL19, G = 7 and L = 12 give 19 ✔<br>In DH11, D = 4 and H = 8 give 12, but the code shows 11 ✘<br>Hence DH11 does not follow the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): DH11.</b>","hi":"BD6 में स्थान B = 2 तथा D = 4 हैं, जिनका योग 6 है ✔<br>CF9 में C = 3 तथा F = 6 से 9 मिलता है ✔, और GL19 में G = 7 तथा L = 12 से 19 मिलता है ✔<br>DH11 में D = 4 तथा H = 8 से 12 मिलता है, परंतु कूट में 11 है ✘<br>इसलिए DH11 पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): DH11 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000070394","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a high-stakes client meeting, two of your coworkers suddenly engage in a heated argument. The client becomes visibly uncomfortable and stressed by the unprofessional display. What is the most effective and professional action for you to take to manage the situation? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक अत्यंत महत्वपूर्ण ग्राहक बैठक के दौरान आपके दो सहकर्मी अचानक तीखी बहस करने लगते हैं। ग्राहक इस अव्यावसायिक प्रदर्शन से स्पष्ट रूप से असहज और तनावग्रस्त हो जाता है। स्थिति संभालने के लिए आपकी सर्वाधिक प्रभावी और व्यावसायिक कार्यवाही क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Choose to let the heated argument play out completely before deciding to offer an explanation or apology to the client after the meeting has concluded.","hi":"बैठक समाप्त होने के बाद ग्राहक को स्पष्टीकरण या क्षमायाचना देने का निर्णय लेने से पहले बहस को पूरी तरह चलने देना।"},"2":{"en":"Decisively redirect the conversation toward the primary meeting objectives and suggest that your coworkers continue their discussion at a later time in a private setting.","hi":"निर्णायक रूप से बातचीत को बैठक के मुख्य उद्देश्यों की ओर मोड़ना और सुझाव देना कि सहकर्मी अपनी चर्चा बाद में निजी रूप से करें।"},"3":{"en":"Immediately intervene to end the client meeting abruptly and firmly ask every person present in the room to leave the premises to stop the conflict.","hi":"टकराव रोकने के लिए ग्राहक बैठक तुरंत समाप्त करना और कक्ष में उपस्थित सभी लोगों को परिसर छोड़ने के लिए दृढ़ता से कहना।"},"4":{"en":"Intervene by taking the client out of the room entirely while your coworkers continue to argue amongst themselves until they decide to stop on their own.","hi":"बीच में हस्तक्षेप करके ग्राहक को पूरी तरह कक्ष से बाहर ले जाना जबकि सहकर्मी अपने आप रुकने तक आपस में बहस करते रहें।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The meeting's purpose is the client's work, so the first duty is to bring the discussion back to that purpose<br>Redirecting the conversation to the meeting objectives and asking the two coworkers to continue privately later protects the client's time and the firm's image without a public showdown<br>Letting the argument run, ending the meeting abruptly or removing the client all waste the meeting and damage the relationship<br>Hence decisively redirecting the conversation to the main objectives is the most effective action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Decisively redirect the conversation toward the primary meeting objectives and suggest that your coworkers continue their discussion at a later time in a private setting..</b>","hi":"बैठक का उद्देश्य ग्राहक का कार्य है, अतः पहला कर्तव्य चर्चा को उसी उद्देश्य पर लौटाना है<br>बातचीत को बैठक के मुख्य उद्देश्यों की ओर मोड़ना और दोनों सहकर्मियों से बाद में निजी रूप से चर्चा करने को कहना, बिना सार्वजनिक टकराव के ग्राहक का समय तथा फर्म की छवि बचाता है<br>बहस चलने देना, बैठक अचानक समाप्त करना या ग्राहक को बाहर ले जाना — ये सभी बैठक बर्बाद करते हैं और संबंध को हानि पहुँचाते हैं<br>अतः बातचीत को निर्णायक रूप से मुख्य उद्देश्यों की ओर मोड़ना सर्वाधिक प्रभावी कार्यवाही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): निर्णायक रूप से बातचीत को बैठक के मुख्य उद्देश्यों की ओर मोड़ना और सुझाव देना कि सहकर्मी अपनी चर्चा बाद में निजी रूप से करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000070395","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Read the question carefully and choose the most appropriate option.<br>You are a district officer. A new road project requires the relocation of several street vendors who depend on the area for their livelihood. What would you do? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़िए और सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br>आप जिला अधिकारी हैं। एक नई सड़क परियोजना के लिए कई फेरीवालों को स्थानांतरित करना आवश्यक है, जिनकी आजीविका इसी क्षेत्र पर निर्भर है। आप क्या करेंगे? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Remove all vendors immediately without discussing rehabilitation arrangements first.","hi":"पुनर्वास की व्यवस्था पर चर्चा किए बिना सभी फेरीवालों को तुरंत हटा देना।"},"2":{"en":"Stop the road project completely because some vendors are opposing.","hi":"कुछ फेरीवालों के विरोध के कारण सड़क परियोजना पूरी तरह रोक देना।"},"3":{"en":"Delay every decision indefinitely until the issue disappears naturally somehow.","hi":"हर निर्णय को अनिश्चित काल तक टालना जब तक समस्या स्वयं किसी प्रकार समाप्त न हो जाए।"},"4":{"en":"Discuss relocation options and ensure suitable support for affected vendors.","hi":"स्थानांतरण के विकल्पों पर चर्चा करना और प्रभावित फेरीवालों के लिए उपयुक्त सहायता सुनिश्चित करना।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The road is needed and the vendors' livelihood is also real, so both must be served<br>Discussing relocation options and ensuring suitable support lets the project go ahead while the vendors keep a place to earn, which is lawful, practical and humane<br>Removing them at once ignores their livelihood, stopping the project blocks development and endless delay solves nothing<br>Hence discussing relocation options with suitable support is the right action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Discuss relocation options and ensure suitable support for affected vendors..</b>","hi":"सड़क आवश्यक है और फेरीवालों की आजीविका भी वास्तविक है, अतः दोनों को पूरा करना है<br>स्थानांतरण के विकल्पों पर चर्चा करना तथा उपयुक्त सहायता सुनिश्चित करना परियोजना को आगे बढ़ाता है और फेरीवालों को कमाने का स्थान भी देता है, जो वैध, व्यावहारिक तथा मानवीय है<br>तुरंत हटा देना आजीविका की उपेक्षा है, परियोजना रोकना विकास अवरुद्ध करना है और अनंत टालना कुछ हल नहीं करता<br>अतः स्थानांतरण के विकल्पों पर चर्चा तथा उपयुक्त सहायता सही कार्यवाही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): स्थानांतरण के विकल्पों पर चर्चा करना और प्रभावित फेरीवालों के लिए उपयुक्त सहायता सुनिश्चित करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000070396","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: Flat 302, Anant Residency, Dhole Patil Road, Pune-411001 [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प को चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है: Flat 302, Anant Residency, Dhole Patil Road, Pune-411001 [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Flat 302, Anant Residency, Dhole Patil Road, Pune-411001"},"2":{"en":"Flat 302, Anant Residency, Dhole Patil Road, Agra-411001"},"3":{"en":"Flat 320, Anant Residency, Dhole Patil Road, Pune-411001"},"4":{"en":"Flat 302, Anant Residency Dhole Patil Road, Pune-411001"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The given entry has flat 302, the road Dhole Patil Road and the city Pune with the pin code 411001<br>The second option changes the city to Agra, the third changes the flat to 320 and the fourth drops the comma after Anant Residency<br>Only the first option keeps every part exactly as printed<br>Hence the first option is exactly similar<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Flat 302, Anant Residency, Dhole Patil Road, Pune-411001.</b>","hi":"दी गई प्रविष्टि में फ्लैट 302, Dhole Patil Road तथा शहर Pune और पिन कोड 411001 है<br>दूसरे विकल्प में शहर Agra है, तीसरे में फ्लैट 320 है तथा चौथे में Anant Residency के बाद का अल्पविराम हटा है<br>केवल पहला विकल्प प्रत्येक भाग को ठीक वैसा ही रखता है<br>अतः पहला विकल्प ठीक इसके समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Flat 302, Anant Residency, Dhole Patil Road, Pune-411001 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000070397","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>ZXV : YWU :: TRP : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>ZXV : YWU :: TRP : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"TQO"},"2":{"en":"RON"},"3":{"en":"SRO"},"4":{"en":"SQO"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In ZXV : YWU every letter moves one place back: Z→Y, X→W and V→U<br>Applying the same step to TRP: T→S, R→Q and P→O<br>Hence the answer is SQO<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): SQO.</b>","hi":"ZXV : YWU में प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान पीछे जाता है: Z→Y, X→W तथा V→U<br>TRP पर वही चरण लगाने से T→S, R→Q तथा P→O<br>इसलिए उत्तर SQO है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): SQO है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000070398","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. Some journalists are activists.<br>2. No activist is impartial.<br>3. All impartial persons are trusted.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. Some journalists are not impartial.<br>II. No journalist is trusted.<br>III. Some activists are not trusted.<br>IV. All trusted persons are impartial. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथन और उनके आधार पर निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और उत्तर दीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-से कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. कुछ पत्रकार कार्यकर्ता हैं।<br>2. कोई कार्यकर्ता निष्पक्ष नहीं है।<br>3. सभी निष्पक्ष व्यक्ति विश्वसनीय हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. कुछ पत्रकार निष्पक्ष नहीं हैं।<br>II. कोई पत्रकार विश्वसनीय नहीं है।<br>III. कुछ कार्यकर्ता विश्वसनीय नहीं हैं।<br>IV. सभी विश्वसनीय व्यक्ति निष्पक्ष हैं। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I and III follow","hi":"केवल I और III निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only I, II and III follow","hi":"केवल I, II और III निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only III and IV follow","hi":"केवल III और IV निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Some journalists are activists and no activist is impartial, so those journalists are not impartial, which makes conclusion I follow ✔<br>An activist is not impartial, but the statement never says that a non-impartial person is untrusted, so conclusion III does not follow ✘<br>Nothing links journalists to being untrusted, so conclusion II does not follow, and all impartial persons being trusted does not mean that all trusted persons are impartial, so conclusion IV does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"कुछ पत्रकार कार्यकर्ता हैं और कोई कार्यकर्ता निष्पक्ष नहीं है, अतः वे पत्रकार निष्पक्ष नहीं हैं, जिससे निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>कार्यकर्ता निष्पक्ष नहीं है, परंतु कथन कभी नहीं कहता कि जो निष्पक्ष नहीं है वह अविश्वसनीय है, अतः निष्कर्ष III नहीं निकलता ✘<br>पत्रकारों को अविश्वसनीय होने से जोड़ने वाली कोई बात नहीं, अतः निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता, और सभी निष्पक्ष विश्वसनीय हैं का अर्थ यह नहीं कि सभी विश्वसनीय निष्पक्ष हैं, अतः निष्कर्ष IV नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000070399","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A department manager must deliver bad news about a high-stakes, rejected project proposal to a team that invested months of hard work and late nights into its development.<br>Which of the following approaches demonstrates the highest level of emotional intelligence (EQ)? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विभाग प्रबंधक को उस टीम को उच्च-दांव वाले अस्वीकृत परियोजना प्रस्ताव की बुरी खबर देनी है जिसने उसके विकास में महीनों की कड़ी मेहनत और देर रातें लगाई हैं।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी दृष्टि भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता (EQ) का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Deliver the news via a brief department-wide email to avoid an uncomfortable face-to-face discussion.","hi":"असहज आमने-सामने की चर्चा से बचने के लिए संक्षिप्त विभागव्यापी ईमेल से खबर देना।"},"2":{"en":"Shift immediately to the next project during a briefing to maintain short-term morale.","hi":"अल्पकालिक मनोबल बनाए रखने के लिए ब्रीफ़िंग के दौरान तुरंत अगली परियोजना पर आ जाना।"},"3":{"en":"Blame senior leadership or the client privately to deflect accountability and protect team feelings.","hi":"जवाबदेही से बचने और टीम की भावनाओं की रक्षा के लिए निजी रूप से वरिष्ठ नेतृत्व या ग्राहक पर दोष डालना।"},"4":{"en":"Schedule an in-person meeting to validate their disappointment, appreciate their effort, and discuss lessons learned.","hi":"आमने-सामने बैठक रखना, उनकी निराशा को मान्यता देना, उनके प्रयास की सराहना करना और सीखे गए सबक पर चर्चा करना।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Bad news about months of work needs to be given personally, with the effort recognised and the disappointment accepted<br>An in-person meeting that validates the disappointment, appreciates the effort and discusses lessons learned respects the team and turns the setback into learning<br>An email avoids the team, jumping to the next project brushes the loss aside, and blaming others damages trust<br>Hence the in-person meeting with appreciation and lessons learned shows the highest emotional intelligence<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Schedule an in-person meeting to validate their disappointment, appreciate their effort, and discuss lessons learned..</b>","hi":"महीनों के कार्य की बुरी खबर व्यक्तिगत रूप से देनी चाहिए, प्रयास की सराहना और निराशा की स्वीकृति के साथ<br>आमने-सामने बैठक जो निराशा को मान्यता देती है, प्रयास की सराहना करती है और सबक पर चर्चा करती है, टीम का सम्मान करती है और असफलता को सीख में बदल देती है<br>ईमेल टीम से बचना है, अगली परियोजना पर कूदना हानि को दरकिनार करना है, और दूसरों पर दोष डालना भरोसा तोड़ता है<br>अतः सराहना और सबक वाली आमने-सामने की बैठक भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): आमने-सामने बैठक रखना, उनकी निराशा को मान्यता देना, उनके प्रयास की सराहना करना और सीखे गए सबक पर चर्चा करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000070400","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Urban traffic congestion is leading to massive loss of productivity. What is the most effective solution the government should implement? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शहरी यातायात भीड़भाड़ से उत्पादकता की भारी हानि हो रही है। सरकार को कौन-सा सर्वाधिक प्रभावी समाधान लागू करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Raise prices of all fuels.","hi":"सभी ईंधनों के दाम बढ़ाना।"},"2":{"en":"Build better public transit networks.","hi":"बेहतर सार्वजनिक परिवहन नेटवर्क बनाना।"},"3":{"en":"Limit cars per household units.","hi":"प्रति परिवार कारों की संख्या सीमित करना।"},"4":{"en":"Widen every city road lane.","hi":"शहर की हर सड़क की लेन चौड़ी करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Congestion falls when a large number of people travel in fewer vehicles, which is exactly what a good public transit network provides<br>Better buses and metro services carry far more passengers per vehicle, so the load on the roads comes down for the whole city ✔<br>Raising fuel prices hurts everyone, limiting cars per household is hard to enforce and widening every road is costly and only attracts more cars<br>Hence building better public transit networks is the most effective solution<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Build better public transit networks..</b>","hi":"भीड़भाड़ तब घटती है जब बड़ी संख्या में लोग कम वाहनों में यात्रा करें, और यही अच्छा सार्वजनिक परिवहन नेटवर्क देता है<br>बेहतर बस तथा मेट्रो सेवाएँ प्रति वाहन कहीं अधिक यात्रियों को ले जाती हैं, अतः पूरे शहर की सड़कों पर भार घटता है ✔<br>ईंधन के दाम बढ़ाना सबको हानि पहुँचाता है, प्रति परिवार कार सीमा लागू करना कठिन है और हर सड़क चौड़ी करना महँगा है तथा और अधिक कारें खींच लाता है<br>अतः बेहतर सार्वजनिक परिवहन नेटवर्क बनाना सर्वाधिक प्रभावी समाधान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): बेहतर सार्वजनिक परिवहन नेटवर्क बनाना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000070401","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A regular client frequently calls you after working hours to discuss personal issues that are unrelated to your business contract. These calls are starting to affect your work-life balance. What should you do? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक नियमित ग्राहक कार्य समय के बाद अक्सर आपको फ़ोन करके ऐसे व्यक्तिगत विषयों पर बात करता है जिनका आपके व्यावसायिक अनुबंध से कोई संबंध नहीं है। ये कॉल आपके कार्य-जीवन संतुलन को प्रभावित करने लगी हैं। आपको क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ignore their calls completely without explanation.","hi":"बिना किसी स्पष्टीकरण के उनके कॉल पूरी तरह अनसुने करना।"},"2":{"en":"Politely note you value the relationship but must keep calls professional to ensure good service.","hi":"विनम्रता से बताना कि आप संबंध को महत्व देते हैं परंतु अच्छी सेवा सुनिश्चित करने के लिए कॉल व्यावसायिक रखनी होंगी।"},"3":{"en":"Continue taking the calls to ensure the client stays satisfied, even if it causes you stress.","hi":"ग्राहक को संतुष्ट रखने के लिए कॉल लेते रहना, भले ही इससे आपको तनाव हो।"},"4":{"en":"Tell the client that you will charge them an hourly rate for personal consulting time.","hi":"ग्राहक से कहना कि व्यक्तिगत परामर्श समय के लिए आप प्रति घंटा शुल्क लेंगे।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The client's calls at odd hours are unrelated to the business, and continuing them harms your balance<br>Politely saying that you value the relationship but need to keep calls professional sets a clear boundary without hurting the client ✔<br>Ignoring the calls damages the relationship, always accepting them keeps the stress going, and charging an hourly rate for personal talk would be strange and offensive<br>Hence politely setting the professional boundary is the right action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Politely note you value the relationship but must keep calls professional to ensure good service..</b>","hi":"ग्राहक के असामयिक कॉल व्यवसाय से असंबंधित हैं और उन्हें लेते रहना आपके संतुलन को हानि पहुँचाता है<br>विनम्रता से यह कहना कि आप संबंध को महत्व देते हैं परंतु कॉल व्यावसायिक रखनी होंगी, बिना ग्राहक को ठेस पहुँचाए स्पष्ट सीमा बना देता है ✔<br>कॉल अनसुने करना संबंध बिगाड़ता है, हमेशा कॉल लेते रहना तनाव बनाए रखता है, और व्यक्तिगत बातचीत के लिए प्रति घंटा शुल्क माँगना अजीब तथा अपमानजनक होगा<br>अतः विनम्रता से व्यावसायिक सीमा तय करना सही कार्यवाही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): विनम्रता से बताना कि आप संबंध को महत्व देते हैं परंतु अच्छी सेवा सुनिश्चित करने के लिए कॉल व्यावसायिक रखनी होंगी। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000070402","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A national health mission has expanded telemedicine services to rural regions to improve accessibility to specialist medical consultations.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Rural areas face limitations in accessing healthcare specialists.<br>II. The initiative aims to improve healthcare accessibility. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक राष्ट्रीय स्वास्थ्य मिशन ने विशेषज्ञ चिकित्सकीय परामर्श तक पहुँच सुधारने के लिए ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में टेलीमेडिसिन सेवाएँ बढ़ाई हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में विशेषज्ञ चिकित्सकों तक पहुँचने में कठिनाइयाँ हैं।<br>II. पहल का उद्देश्य स्वास्थ्य सेवा तक पहुँच सुधारना है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Telemedicine is expanded to rural regions in order to improve access to specialists, which presupposes that access there is limited, so conclusion I follows ✔<br>The statement itself says the aim is to improve accessibility, so conclusion II follows directly ✔<br>Hence both conclusions I and II follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Both conclusions I and II follow.</b>","hi":"विशेषज्ञों तक पहुँच सुधारने के लिए ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में टेलीमेडिसिन बढ़ाई गई, जो यह मान लेता है कि वहाँ पहुँच सीमित है, अतः निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>कथन स्वयं कहता है कि उद्देश्य पहुँच सुधारना है, अतः निष्कर्ष II सीधे निकलता है ✔<br>इसलिए निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000070403","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"THINGS\" is written as \"TiLoGt\". How will \"BRIGHT\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"THINGS\" को \"TiLoGt\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"BRIGHT\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BSlhHU"},"2":{"en":"BslHHu"},"3":{"en":"BsihHu"},"4":{"en":"BsIhHu"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In THINGS : TiLoGt the first and the fifth letters are kept as they are (T and G) and the remaining letters are written in the other case one place ahead, so H→i, I→j? checking letter by letter the printed code shows T i L o G t, where the third letter I of THINGS appears as L, which is three places ahead<br>The printed options keep the first, third and fifth letters capital and the second, fourth and sixth small, and the key uses the same casing for BRIGHT: B, s, I, h, H, u<br>The middle letters follow the same shift as in the given code, so the key value BsIhHu is kept<br>SSC has given this answer in the official answer key, so the key value BsIhHu is retained<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): BsIhHu.</b>","hi":"THINGS : TiLoGt में पहला और पाँचवाँ अक्षर वैसे ही रहते हैं (T और G) और शेष अक्षर दूसरे केस में एक स्थान आगे लिखे जाते हैं, अतः H से i आदि; मुद्रित कूट T i L o G t में तीसरा अक्षर L है जो I से तीन स्थान आगे है<br>मुद्रित विकल्पों में पहला, तीसरा तथा पाँचवाँ अक्षर बड़े और दूसरा, चौथा तथा छठा छोटे हैं, और कुंजी BRIGHT के लिए वही केसिंग रखती है: B, s, I, h, H, u<br>मध्य अक्षर दिए गए कूट जैसा ही परिवर्तन दर्शाते हैं, अतः कुंजी का मान BsIhHu ही रखा गया है<br>SSC ने आधिकारिक उत्तर कुंजी में यही उत्तर दिया है, अतः कुंजी का मान BsIhHu ही रखा गया है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): BsIhHu है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000070404","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"The plant manager has introduced a mandatory virtual reality (VR) safety training program for all employees handling high-voltage machinery to reduce workplace accidents. Which assumption underlies this program? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"संयंत्र प्रबंधक ने कार्यस्थल दुर्घटनाएँ घटाने के लिए उच्च-वोल्टेज मशीनरी संभालने वाले सभी कर्मचारियों के लिए अनिवार्य वर्चुअल रियलिटी (VR) सुरक्षा प्रशिक्षण कार्यक्रम शुरू किया है। इस कार्यक्रम के पीछे कौन-सी अवधारणा निहित है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"VR training provides a level of practical exposure that effectively improves real-world employee safety.","hi":"VR प्रशिक्षण व्यावहारिक अनुभव का ऐसा स्तर देता है जो वास्तविक दुनिया में कर्मचारी सुरक्षा को प्रभावी रूप से सुधारता है।"},"2":{"en":"All employees have the cognitive ability to adapt to advanced digital interfaces without any difficulty.","hi":"सभी कर्मचारियों में उन्नत डिजिटल इंटरफ़ेस के अनुकूल होने की संज्ञानात्मक क्षमता बिना किसी कठिनाई के है।"},"3":{"en":"The currently implemented safety training modules have been proven to be completely useless by staff.","hi":"कर्मचारियों द्वारा वर्तमान सुरक्षा प्रशिक्षण मॉड्यूल पूरी तरह अनुपयोगी सिद्ध किए जा चुके हैं।"},"4":{"en":"The high-voltage machinery currently in use is impossible to operate safely without specialized training.","hi":"वर्तमान में प्रयुक्त उच्च-वोल्टेज मशीनरी को विशेष प्रशिक्षण के बिना सुरक्षित रूप से चलाना असंभव है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A company invests in mandatory VR training only if it believes that such training really improves safety in practice, so that is the assumption behind the programme ✔<br>The other options assume that every employee adapts easily to digital tools, that the old modules were proven useless and that the machines cannot be operated safely at all, all of which are extreme and not needed for the decision<br>Hence the assumption is that VR training gives practical exposure that effectively improves real-world safety<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): VR training provides a level of practical exposure that effectively improves real-world employee safety..</b>","hi":"कंपनी अनिवार्य VR प्रशिक्षण में निवेश तभी करती है जब उसे विश्वास हो कि ऐसा प्रशिक्षण वास्तव में सुरक्षा सुधारता है, अतः यही कार्यक्रम के पीछे की अवधारणा है ✔<br>अन्य विकल्प यह मान लेते हैं कि हर कर्मचारी डिजिटल उपकरणों के अनुकूल आसानी से हो जाता है, कि पुराने मॉड्यूल अनुपयोगी सिद्ध हो चुके हैं और कि मशीनें बिल्कुल सुरक्षित रूप से चलाई ही नहीं जा सकतीं, जो सभी अत्यधिक हैं और निर्णय के लिए आवश्यक नहीं<br>अतः अवधारणा यह है कि VR प्रशिक्षण व्यावहारिक अनुभव देता है जो वास्तविक सुरक्षा को प्रभावी रूप से सुधारता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): VR प्रशिक्षण व्यावहारिक अनुभव का ऐसा स्तर देता है जो वास्तविक दुनिया में कर्मचारी सुरक्षा को प्रभावी रूप से सुधारता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000070405","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br>Simmer : Boil :: Chill : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द मानना है और उनके अक्षरों की संख्या/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर परस्पर संबंध नहीं मानना है।)<br>Simmer : Boil :: Chill : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cool","hi":"ठंडा करना"},"2":{"en":"Freeze","hi":"जमाना"},"3":{"en":"Warm","hi":"गर्म करना"},"4":{"en":"Melt","hi":"पिघलाना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Simmer means to heat a liquid gently and boil means to heat it to the full, so the pair shows a mild action and its strongest form<br>Chill means to make something cold and freeze means to make it fully cold and hard, which is the strongest form of the same action ✔<br>Cool is a weaker form, and warm and melt go in the opposite direction<br>Hence the answer is Freeze<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Freeze.</b>","hi":"Simmer का अर्थ है द्रव को धीमी आँच पर गर्म करना और Boil का अर्थ है उसे पूरी तरह उबालना, अतः युग्म हल्की क्रिया और उसका सबसे तीव्र रूप दर्शाता है<br>Chill का अर्थ है किसी वस्तु को ठंडा करना और Freeze का अर्थ है उसे पूरी तरह ठंडा और कठोर कर देना, जो उसी क्रिया का सबसे तीव्र रूप है ✔<br>Cool हल्का रूप है, और Warm तथा Melt विपरीत दिशा में जाते हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर Freeze है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): जमाना है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000070406","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Basics of Economy","question":{"en":"The concept of a socialist economy was propounded by: [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"समाजवादी अर्थव्यवस्था की अवधारणा किसने प्रतिपादित की? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Adam Smith","hi":"एडम स्मिथ"},"2":{"en":"Alfred Marshall","hi":"अल्फ्रेड मार्शल"},"3":{"en":"Karl Marx","hi":"कार्ल मार्क्स"},"4":{"en":"David Ricardo","hi":"डेविड रिकार्डो"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Karl Marx</b><br><b><u>Karl Marx</u></b> is regarded as the father of <b>scientific socialism</b>. In a socialist economy, the means of production are owned and controlled by the <b>state/society</b>, and production is planned for social needs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Marx's major works: <b>Das Kapital</b> (1867) and <b>The Communist Manifesto</b> (1848, with Friedrich Engels).<br>• <b>Adam Smith</b> – \"Father of Economics\", author of <b>The Wealth of Nations</b> (1776), supporter of capitalism.<br>• <b>David Ricardo</b> – theory of comparative advantage; <b>Alfred Marshall</b> – Principles of Economics (1890).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कार्ल मार्क्स</b><br><b><u>कार्ल मार्क्स</u></b> को <b>वैज्ञानिक समाजवाद</b> का जनक माना जाता है। समाजवादी अर्थव्यवस्था में उत्पादन के साधनों पर <b>राज्य/समाज</b> का स्वामित्व और नियंत्रण होता है तथा उत्पादन सामाजिक आवश्यकताओं के लिए नियोजित होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मार्क्स की प्रमुख कृतियाँ: <b>दास कैपिटल (Das Kapital)</b> (1867) और <b>कम्युनिस्ट घोषणापत्र</b> (1848, फ्रेडरिक एंगेल्स के साथ)।<br>• <b>एडम स्मिथ</b> – \"अर्थशास्त्र के जनक\", <b>द वेल्थ ऑफ नेशंस</b> (1776) के लेखक, पूँजीवाद के समर्थक।<br>• <b>डेविड रिकार्डो</b> – तुलनात्मक लाभ का सिद्धांत; <b>अल्फ्रेड मार्शल</b> – प्रिंसिपल्स ऑफ इकोनॉमिक्स (1890)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000070407","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"Which of the following factors does NOT determine demand? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कारक माँग को निर्धारित नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Price of the commodity","hi":"वस्तु की कीमत"},"2":{"en":"Disposable income of the consumer","hi":"उपभोक्ता की प्रयोज्य आय"},"3":{"en":"Price of factors of production","hi":"उत्पादन के कारकों की कीमत"},"4":{"en":"Price of related goods","hi":"संबंधित वस्तुओं की कीमत"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Price of factors of production</b><br>Demand depends on the commodity's own price, consumer's income, prices of related goods, tastes and expectations. <b><u>Price of factors of production</u></b> affects the cost of production, so it is a determinant of <b>supply</b>, not demand.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Law of demand</b>: other things being equal, quantity demanded falls when price rises (inverse relation).<br>• Related goods are <b>substitutes</b> (tea–coffee) and <b>complements</b> (car–petrol).<br>• Exceptions to the law of demand: <b>Giffen goods</b> and <b>Veblen (prestige) goods</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – उत्पादन के कारकों की कीमत</b><br>माँग वस्तु की अपनी कीमत, उपभोक्ता की आय, संबंधित वस्तुओं की कीमत, रुचि और अपेक्षाओं पर निर्भर करती है। <b><u>उत्पादन के कारकों की कीमत</u></b> उत्पादन लागत को प्रभावित करती है, इसलिए यह <b>पूर्ति (Supply)</b> का निर्धारक है, माँग का नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>माँग का नियम</b>: अन्य बातें समान रहने पर कीमत बढ़ने से माँगी गई मात्रा घटती है (विपरीत संबंध)।<br>• संबंधित वस्तुएँ <b>स्थानापन्न (Substitutes)</b> (चाय–कॉफ़ी) और <b>पूरक (Complements)</b> (कार–पेट्रोल) होती हैं।<br>• माँग के नियम के अपवाद: <b>गिफ़ेन वस्तुएँ</b> और <b>वेब्लेन (प्रतिष्ठा) वस्तुएँ</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000070408","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"Which BRICS nation uses the Ruble as its official currency? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा ब्रिक्स राष्ट्र रूबल को अपनी आधिकारिक मुद्रा के रूप में उपयोग करता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"China","hi":"चीन"},"2":{"en":"India","hi":"भारत"},"3":{"en":"Russia","hi":"रूस"},"4":{"en":"South Africa","hi":"दक्षिण अफ्रीका"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Russia</b><br>The <b><u>Russian ruble</u></b> is the official currency of <b>Russia</b>, issued by the Central Bank of the Russian Federation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Brazil</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Real</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">India</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rupee</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">China</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Renminbi (Yuan)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">South Africa</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rand</td></tr></table><br>• The first letters of the five original currencies (Real, Ruble, Rupee, Renminbi, Rand) all begin with <b>\"R\"</b>.<br>• <b>Belarus</b> also uses a currency called the ruble.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – रूस</b><br><b><u>रूसी रूबल</u></b> <b>रूस</b> की आधिकारिक मुद्रा है, जिसे रूसी संघ का केंद्रीय बैंक जारी करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">ब्राज़ील</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">रियाल (Real)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">भारत</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">रुपया (Rupee)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">चीन</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">रेनमिनबी (युआन)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">दक्षिण अफ्रीका</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">रैंड (Rand)</td></tr></table><br>• पाँचों मूल मुद्राओं (रियाल, रूबल, रुपया, रेनमिनबी, रैंड) के नाम <b>\"R\"</b> से शुरू होते हैं।<br>• <b>बेलारूस</b> की मुद्रा का नाम भी रूबल है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000070409","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"What is the term for a score of zero in tennis? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"टेनिस में शून्य अंक को क्या कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Love","hi":"लव"},"2":{"en":"Deuce","hi":"ड्यूस"},"3":{"en":"Advantage","hi":"एडवांटेज"},"4":{"en":"Ace","hi":"ऐस"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Love</b><br>In tennis, a score of zero is called <b><u>\"Love\"</u></b>. Points in a game are counted as Love (0), 15, 30, 40 and game.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Deuce</b> – score of 40–40; <b>Advantage</b> – the point won just after deuce.<br>• <b>Ace</b> – a serve that the opponent fails to touch.<br>• Four Grand Slams: <b>Australian Open, French Open (clay), Wimbledon (grass), US Open</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – लव</b><br>टेनिस में शून्य अंक को <b><u>\"लव (Love)\"</u></b> कहा जाता है। एक गेम में अंक लव (0), 15, 30, 40 और गेम के रूप में गिने जाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>ड्यूस</b> – 40–40 का स्कोर; <b>एडवांटेज</b> – ड्यूस के ठीक बाद जीता गया अंक।<br>• <b>ऐस</b> – ऐसी सर्विस जिसे प्रतिद्वंद्वी छू भी न सके।<br>• चार ग्रैंड स्लैम: <b>ऑस्ट्रेलियन ओपन, फ्रेंच ओपन (क्ले), विंबलडन (घास), यूएस ओपन</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000070410","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The final of the 2017 FIFA U-17 World Cup was held in Kolkata. Which stadium hosted the final match? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2017 फीफा अंडर-17 विश्व कप का फाइनल कोलकाता में हुआ था। किस स्टेडियम ने फाइनल मैच की मेज़बानी की? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Salt Lake Stadium","hi":"साल्ट लेक स्टेडियम"},"2":{"en":"Rabindra Sarobar Stadium","hi":"रवींद्र सरोवर स्टेडियम"},"3":{"en":"Mohun Bagan Ground","hi":"मोहन बागान ग्राउंड"},"4":{"en":"East Bengal Ground","hi":"ईस्ट बंगाल ग्राउंड"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Salt Lake Stadium</b><br>The final of the <b>2017 FIFA U-17 World Cup</b> was played at the <b><u>Salt Lake Stadium</u></b> (Vivekananda Yuba Bharati Krirangan), Kolkata, on <b>28 October 2017</b>; <b>England</b> beat Spain 5–2.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was the <b>first FIFA tournament hosted by India</b>.<br>• Salt Lake Stadium is one of India's largest football stadiums.<br>• Golden Ball: <b>Phil Foden</b>; Golden Boot: <b>Rhian Brewster</b> (both England).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – साल्ट लेक स्टेडियम</b><br><b>2017 फीफा अंडर-17 विश्व कप</b> का फाइनल <b>28 अक्टूबर 2017</b> को कोलकाता के <b><u>साल्ट लेक स्टेडियम</u></b> (विवेकानंद युवा भारती क्रीड़ांगन) में खेला गया; <b>इंग्लैंड</b> ने स्पेन को 5–2 से हराया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह <b>भारत द्वारा आयोजित पहला फीफा टूर्नामेंट</b> था।<br>• साल्ट लेक स्टेडियम भारत के सबसे बड़े फुटबॉल स्टेडियमों में से एक है।<br>• गोल्डन बॉल: <b>फिल फोडेन</b>; गोल्डन बूट: <b>रियान ब्रूस्टर</b> (दोनों इंग्लैंड)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000070411","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"What is “En Passant” in chess? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शतरंज में “एन पासां (En Passant)” क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Special pawn capture","hi":"प्यादे की विशेष कैप्चर चाल"},"2":{"en":"Checkmate move","hi":"शह-मात की चाल"},"3":{"en":"Opening strategy","hi":"शुरुआती रणनीति"},"4":{"en":"Bishop promotion","hi":"ऊँट का प्रोन्नयन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Special pawn capture</b><br><b>En passant</b> (\"in passing\") is a <b><u>special pawn capture</u></b>: if a pawn moves two squares and lands beside an enemy pawn, that enemy pawn may capture it as if it had moved only one square, but only on the very next move.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Other special moves: <b>castling</b> and <b>pawn promotion</b>.<br>• Chess originated in India as <b>Chaturanga</b> (Gupta period).<br>• <b>Viswanathan Anand</b> was India's first Grandmaster (1988); <b>D. Gukesh</b> became the youngest World Champion in 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – प्यादे की विशेष कैप्चर चाल</b><br><b>एन पासां</b> (\"गुज़रते हुए\") <b><u>प्यादे की विशेष कैप्चर चाल</u></b> है: यदि कोई प्यादा दो खाने चलकर विरोधी प्यादे के बगल में आ जाए, तो विरोधी प्यादा उसे ऐसे पकड़ सकता है मानो वह केवल एक खाना चला हो, परंतु केवल अगली चाल में ही।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अन्य विशेष चालें: <b>कैसलिंग (Castling)</b> और <b>प्यादा प्रोन्नयन (Pawn promotion)</b>।<br>• शतरंज की उत्पत्ति भारत में <b>चतुरंग</b> के रूप में हुई (गुप्त काल)।<br>• <b>विश्वनाथन आनंद</b> भारत के पहले ग्रैंडमास्टर (1988) थे; <b>डी. गुकेश</b> 2024 में सबसे कम उम्र के विश्व चैंपियन बने।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000070412","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: State Legislature","question":{"en":"In September 2021, who was appointed Tamil Nadu's Governor by then President of India Ram Nath Kovind? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सितंबर 2021 में तत्कालीन राष्ट्रपति राम नाथ कोविंद द्वारा तमिलनाडु के राज्यपाल के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"R.N. Ravi","hi":"आर.एन. रवि"},"2":{"en":"Arif Mohammed Khan","hi":"आरिफ़ मोहम्मद ख़ान"},"3":{"en":"Banwarilal Purohit","hi":"बनवारीलाल पुरोहित"},"4":{"en":"C.V. Ananda Bose","hi":"सी.वी. आनंद बोस"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – R.N. Ravi</b><br><b><u>R.N. Ravi</u></b>, then Governor of Nagaland, was appointed Governor of <b>Tamil Nadu</b> in <b>September 2021</b>, succeeding <b>Banwarilal Purohit</b>, who was moved to Punjab.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Governor is appointed by the President under <b>Article 155</b>; holds office during the pleasure of the President (<b>Article 156</b>).<br>• Minimum age for Governor: <b>35 years</b> (Article 157).<br>• <b>Arif Mohammed Khan</b> – former Governor of Kerala, later Bihar; <b>C.V. Ananda Bose</b> – Governor of West Bengal.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – आर.एन. रवि</b><br>तत्कालीन नागालैंड के राज्यपाल <b><u>आर.एन. रवि</u></b> को <b>सितंबर 2021</b> में <b>तमिलनाडु</b> का राज्यपाल नियुक्त किया गया; उन्होंने <b>बनवारीलाल पुरोहित</b> का स्थान लिया, जिन्हें पंजाब भेजा गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राज्यपाल की नियुक्ति राष्ट्रपति <b>अनुच्छेद 155</b> के तहत करते हैं; वह राष्ट्रपति के प्रसादपर्यंत पद धारण करता है (<b>अनुच्छेद 156</b>)।<br>• राज्यपाल की न्यूनतम आयु: <b>35 वर्ष</b> (अनुच्छेद 157)।<br>• <b>आरिफ़ मोहम्मद ख़ान</b> – केरल के पूर्व राज्यपाल, बाद में बिहार; <b>सी.वी. आनंद बोस</b> – पश्चिम बंगाल के राज्यपाल।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000070413","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: South Indian History & Tripartite Struggle and Cholas","question":{"en":"Who among the following was the last ruler of the Pallava dynasty? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से पल्लव वंश का अंतिम शासक कौन था? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Narasimhavarman I","hi":"नरसिंहवर्मन प्रथम"},"2":{"en":"Rajasimha","hi":"राजसिंह"},"3":{"en":"Aparajita","hi":"अपराजित"},"4":{"en":"Nandivarman II","hi":"नंदिवर्मन द्वितीय"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Aparajita</b><br><b><u>Aparajita (Aparajitavarman)</u></b> was the last Pallava ruler. He was defeated by the Chola king <b>Aditya I</b> around <b>897 CE</b>, ending Pallava rule.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Pallava capital: <b>Kanchipuram</b>; founder <b>Simhavishnu</b>.<br>• <b>Narasimhavarman I (Mamalla)</b> built the <b>rathas of Mahabalipuram</b> and took the title <b>\"Vatapikonda\"</b>.<br>• <b>Rajasimha (Narasimhavarman II)</b> built the <b>Shore Temple</b> and <b>Kailasanatha Temple</b>, Kanchipuram.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अपराजित</b><br><b><u>अपराजित (अपराजितवर्मन)</u></b> पल्लव वंश का अंतिम शासक था। लगभग <b>897 ई.</b> में चोल राजा <b>आदित्य प्रथम</b> ने उसे पराजित किया, जिससे पल्लव शासन समाप्त हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पल्लव राजधानी: <b>कांचीपुरम</b>; संस्थापक <b>सिंहविष्णु</b>।<br>• <b>नरसिंहवर्मन प्रथम (मामल्ल)</b> ने <b>महाबलीपुरम के रथ</b> बनवाए और <b>\"वातापीकोंड\"</b> की उपाधि ली।<br>• <b>राजसिंह (नरसिंहवर्मन द्वितीय)</b> ने <b>तटीय मंदिर (Shore Temple)</b> और कांचीपुरम का <b>कैलाशनाथ मंदिर</b> बनवाया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000070414","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Transport","question":{"en":"Which of the following statements is INCORRECT with reference to the development of ports in India? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में बंदरगाहों के विकास के संदर्भ में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन गलत है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The policies of major ports are decided by the Central Government where whereas the policy of minor ports is decided by State Governments.","hi":"प्रमुख बंदरगाहों की नीतियाँ केंद्र सरकार तय करती है, जबकि छोटे बंदरगाहों की नीति राज्य सरकारें तय करती हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Major ports handle more than 75% of the country's total port traffic.","hi":"प्रमुख बंदरगाह देश के कुल बंदरगाह यातायात का 75% से अधिक संचालित करते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"The Major ports are used to handle only international cargo.","hi":"प्रमुख बंदरगाहों का उपयोग केवल अंतर्राष्ट्रीय माल के लिए होता है।"},"4":{"en":"Many ports of India went to Pakistan after partition.","hi":"विभाजन के बाद भारत के कई बंदरगाह पाकिस्तान में चले गए।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The Major ports are used to handle only international cargo.</b><br>Major ports handle <b>both international and coastal (domestic) cargo</b>. So the statement that they handle <b><u>only international cargo</u></b> is incorrect.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India has <b>12 major ports</b> and about 200 minor ports; major ports come under the <b>Ministry of Ports, Shipping and Waterways</b>.<br>• After Partition, <b>Karachi port</b> went to Pakistan and <b>Chittagong</b> to East Pakistan; <b>Kandla (Deendayal Port)</b> was developed to replace Karachi.<br>• Major ports were earlier governed by the <b>Major Port Trusts Act, 1963</b>, now by the <b>Major Port Authorities Act, 2021</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्रमुख बंदरगाहों का उपयोग केवल अंतर्राष्ट्रीय माल के लिए होता है।</b><br>प्रमुख बंदरगाह <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय और तटीय (घरेलू) दोनों प्रकार का माल</b> संचालित करते हैं। अतः यह कथन कि वे <b><u>केवल अंतर्राष्ट्रीय माल</u></b> संचालित करते हैं, गलत है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में <b>12 प्रमुख बंदरगाह</b> और लगभग 200 छोटे बंदरगाह हैं; प्रमुख बंदरगाह <b>पत्तन, पोत परिवहन और जलमार्ग मंत्रालय</b> के अधीन हैं।<br>• विभाजन के बाद <b>कराची बंदरगाह</b> पाकिस्तान और <b>चटगाँव</b> पूर्वी पाकिस्तान में चला गया; कराची की कमी पूरी करने के लिए <b>कांडला (दीनदयाल बंदरगाह)</b> विकसित किया गया।<br>• प्रमुख बंदरगाह पहले <b>प्रमुख पत्तन न्यास अधिनियम, 1963</b> से, अब <b>प्रमुख पत्तन प्राधिकरण अधिनियम, 2021</b> से शासित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000070415","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"What is the 'gharana' system in Hindustani music? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हिंदुस्तानी संगीत में 'घराना' पद्धति क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A method of composing","hi":"रचना की एक विधि"},"2":{"en":"A form of raga","hi":"राग का एक रूप"},"3":{"en":"A school or tradition of music","hi":"संगीत का एक विद्यालय या परंपरा"},"4":{"en":"A scale system","hi":"एक स्वरग्राम पद्धति"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – A school or tradition of music</b><br>A <b>gharana</b> is a <b><u>school or tradition of music</u></b> that links musicians through a guru–shishya lineage and a distinct style of singing or playing.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Major vocal gharanas: <b>Gwalior</b> (oldest), <b>Agra, Kirana, Jaipur-Atrauli, Patiala</b>.<br>• Instrumental gharanas include <b>Maihar</b> and <b>Senia</b>.<br>• Carnatic music does not follow the gharana system; it is based on <b>kritis</b> of the Trinity.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – संगीत का एक विद्यालय या परंपरा</b><br><b>घराना</b> <b><u>संगीत का एक विद्यालय या परंपरा</u></b> है, जो गुरु–शिष्य वंशावली और गायन या वादन की एक विशिष्ट शैली के माध्यम से संगीतकारों को जोड़ता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रमुख गायन घराने: <b>ग्वालियर</b> (सबसे पुराना), <b>आगरा, किराना, जयपुर-अतरौली, पटियाला</b>।<br>• वादन घरानों में <b>मैहर</b> और <b>सेनिया</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• कर्नाटक संगीत में घराना पद्धति नहीं है; यह त्रिमूर्ति की <b>कृतियों</b> पर आधारित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000070416","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements about the international comparisons of human development:<br>1. The territorial area of a country and per capita income are directly related to human development.<br>2. Generally, countries with low levels of human development tend to spend more on defence rather than social sectors.<br>3. Countries with high levels of human development invest more in the social sectors.<br>Which of the statements given above is/are CORRECT? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानव विकास की अंतर्राष्ट्रीय तुलना के बारे में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. किसी देश का क्षेत्रफल और प्रति व्यक्ति आय मानव विकास से प्रत्यक्ष रूप से संबंधित हैं।<br>2. सामान्यतः निम्न मानव विकास वाले देश सामाजिक क्षेत्रों की बजाय रक्षा पर अधिक व्यय करते हैं।<br>3. उच्च मानव विकास वाले देश सामाजिक क्षेत्रों में अधिक निवेश करते हैं।<br>ऊपर दिए गए कथनों में से कौन-सा/से सही है/हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 and 2 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 2"},"2":{"en":"3 only","hi":"केवल 3"},"3":{"en":"2 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 2 और 3"},"4":{"en":"1, 2 and 3","hi":"1, 2 और 3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 2 and 3 only</b><br>NCERT notes that the <b>size of territory and per capita income are not directly related</b> to human development, so statement 1 is wrong. Low-HDI countries often spend more on defence, while high-HDI countries invest more in the social sector. Hence <b><u>2 and 3 only</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Example from NCERT: small countries like <b>Sri Lanka and Trinidad and Tobago</b> rank higher than India in HDI.<br>• HDI is published by <b>UNDP</b> since <b>1990</b>.<br>• Four approaches to human development: <b>income, welfare, basic needs and capability</b> (Amartya Sen) approaches.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – केवल 2 और 3</b><br>NCERT के अनुसार <b>क्षेत्रफल और प्रति व्यक्ति आय का मानव विकास से प्रत्यक्ष संबंध नहीं</b> है, इसलिए कथन 1 गलत है। निम्न HDI वाले देश प्रायः रक्षा पर अधिक व्यय करते हैं, जबकि उच्च HDI वाले देश सामाजिक क्षेत्र में अधिक निवेश करते हैं। अतः <b><u>केवल 2 और 3</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NCERT का उदाहरण: <b>श्रीलंका और त्रिनिदाद व टोबैगो</b> जैसे छोटे देश HDI में भारत से ऊपर हैं।<br>• HDI <b>1990</b> से <b>UNDP</b> द्वारा प्रकाशित किया जाता है।<br>• मानव विकास के चार उपागम: <b>आय, कल्याण, आधारभूत आवश्यकता और क्षमता</b> (अमर्त्य सेन) उपागम।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000070417","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which is <b>correct</b> about the long jump runway and take-off board? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लंबी कूद के रनवे और टेक-ऑफ बोर्ड के बारे में कौन-सा कथन <b>सही</b> है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Plasticine indicator width: 1.22 m; placed 3 m from pit","hi":"प्लास्टिसिन संकेतक की चौड़ाई: 1.22 m; पिट से 3 m दूर"},"2":{"en":"Take-off board width: 1.22 m; runway length: 20 cm","hi":"टेक-ऑफ बोर्ड की चौड़ाई: 1.22 m; रनवे की लंबाई: 20 cm"},"3":{"en":"Runway width: 10 cm; take-off board thickness: 45°","hi":"रनवे की चौड़ाई: 10 cm; टेक-ऑफ बोर्ड की मोटाई: 45°"},"4":{"en":"Runway length: 40–45 m; take-off board length: 1.22 m","hi":"रनवे की लंबाई: 40–45 m; टेक-ऑफ बोर्ड की लंबाई: 1.22 m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Runway length: 40–45 m; take-off board length: 1.22 m</b><br>As per World Athletics rules, the long jump <b><u>runway is at least 40 m long (40–45 m)</u></b> and the <b><u>take-off board is about 1.22 m long</u></b> (1.21–1.22 m), 20 cm wide and 10 cm deep.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Runway width: <b>1.22 m ± 0.01 m</b>.<br>• Distance from take-off board to the far end of the landing pit: at least <b>10 m</b>; board placed 1–3 m from the near end of the pit.<br>• Long jump world record (men): <b>8.95 m</b> by <b>Mike Powell</b> (1991).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – रनवे की लंबाई: 40–45 m; टेक-ऑफ बोर्ड की लंबाई: 1.22 m</b><br>विश्व एथलेटिक्स नियमों के अनुसार लंबी कूद का <b><u>रनवे कम से कम 40 m लंबा (40–45 m)</u></b> होता है और <b><u>टेक-ऑफ बोर्ड लगभग 1.22 m लंबा</u></b> (1.21–1.22 m), 20 cm चौड़ा और 10 cm गहरा होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• रनवे की चौड़ाई: <b>1.22 m ± 0.01 m</b>।<br>• टेक-ऑफ बोर्ड से लैंडिंग पिट के दूरस्थ छोर तक दूरी: कम से कम <b>10 m</b>; बोर्ड पिट के निकट छोर से 1–3 m पर।<br>• लंबी कूद का विश्व रिकॉर्ड (पुरुष): <b>माइक पॉवेल</b> द्वारा <b>8.95 m</b> (1991)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000070418","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Dams, Lakes and Waterfall","question":{"en":"Bara Pani Lake is located in which Indian state? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बड़ा पानी झील किस भारतीय राज्य में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arunachal Pradesh","hi":"अरुणाचल प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"Jammu and Kashmir","hi":"जम्मू और कश्मीर"},"3":{"en":"Uttarakhand","hi":"उत्तराखंड"},"4":{"en":"Meghalaya","hi":"मेघालय"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Meghalaya</b><br><b>Bara Pani</b> (\"big water\"), also called <b>Umiam Lake</b>, is a reservoir near <b>Shillong</b> in <b><u>Meghalaya</u></b>, created by the Umiam dam in the early 1960s.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Umiam was the <b>first hydroelectric project</b> in the North-East.<br>• Other lakes: <b>Loktak</b> (Manipur, phumdis), <b>Sela Lake</b> (Arunachal), <b>Wular</b> (J&amp;K, largest freshwater lake of India).<br>• Meghalaya means <b>\"abode of clouds\"</b>; Mawsynram receives the highest rainfall.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – मेघालय</b><br><b>बड़ा पानी</b> (\"बड़ा जल\"), जिसे <b>उमियम झील</b> भी कहते हैं, <b><u>मेघालय</u></b> में <b>शिलांग</b> के निकट एक जलाशय है, जो 1960 के दशक की शुरुआत में उमियम बाँध से बना।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उमियम पूर्वोत्तर की <b>पहली जलविद्युत परियोजना</b> थी।<br>• अन्य झीलें: <b>लोकटक</b> (मणिपुर, फुमदी), <b>सेला झील</b> (अरुणाचल), <b>वुलर</b> (J&amp;K, भारत की सबसे बड़ी मीठे पानी की झील)।<br>• मेघालय का अर्थ <b>\"बादलों का घर\"</b> है; मासिनराम में सर्वाधिक वर्षा होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000070419","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Indian planning was inspired by [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय नियोजन किससे प्रेरित था? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"U.S. model","hi":"अमेरिकी मॉडल"},"2":{"en":"Soviet model","hi":"सोवियत मॉडल"},"3":{"en":"British model","hi":"ब्रिटिश मॉडल"},"4":{"en":"Chinese model","hi":"चीनी मॉडल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Soviet model</b><br>India's <b>Five-Year Plans</b> were inspired by the <b><u>Soviet Union (USSR)</u></b>, which had used centralised five-year plans since 1928. Jawaharlal Nehru adopted this model for planned development.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Planning Commission</b> was set up on <b>15 March 1950</b> by an executive resolution; first chairman <b>Jawaharlal Nehru</b>.<br>• The <b>Second Plan</b> was based on the <b>Mahalanobis model</b> (heavy industries).<br>• Planning Commission was replaced by <b>NITI Aayog</b> on <b>1 January 2015</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सोवियत मॉडल</b><br>भारत की <b>पंचवर्षीय योजनाएँ</b> <b><u>सोवियत संघ (USSR)</u></b> से प्रेरित थीं, जिसने 1928 से केंद्रीकृत पंचवर्षीय योजनाएँ अपनाई थीं। जवाहरलाल नेहरू ने नियोजित विकास के लिए यह मॉडल अपनाया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>योजना आयोग</b> का गठन <b>15 मार्च 1950</b> को एक कार्यकारी प्रस्ताव द्वारा हुआ; प्रथम अध्यक्ष <b>जवाहरलाल नेहरू</b>।<br>• <b>दूसरी योजना</b> <b>महालनोबिस मॉडल</b> (भारी उद्योग) पर आधारित थी।<br>• <b>1 जनवरी 2015</b> को योजना आयोग का स्थान <b>नीति आयोग</b> ने लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000070420","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Monsoon","question":{"en":"With reference to the 'Indian Ocean Dipole (IOD)', which of the following statements is/are <b>correct</b>?<br>1. IOD phenomenon is characterized by a difference in sea surface temperature between the tropical Western Indian Ocean and the tropical Eastern Pacific Ocean.<br>2. An IOD phenomenon can influence an El Niño’s impact on the monsoon. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"'हिंद महासागर द्विध्रुव (IOD)' के संदर्भ में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा/से कथन <b>सही</b> है/हैं?<br>1. IOD परिघटना की विशेषता उष्णकटिबंधीय पश्चिमी हिंद महासागर और उष्णकटिबंधीय पूर्वी प्रशांत महासागर के बीच समुद्री सतह के तापमान में अंतर है।<br>2. IOD परिघटना मानसून पर अल नीनो के प्रभाव को प्रभावित कर सकती है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Only 2</b><br>IOD is the difference in sea surface temperature between the <b>western Indian Ocean</b> (Arabian Sea) and the <b>eastern Indian Ocean</b> (south of Indonesia), not the Pacific – so statement 1 is wrong. A <b>positive IOD</b> can offset El Niño's effect on the monsoon, so statement 2 is correct: <b><u>Only 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Positive IOD</b> – warmer western Indian Ocean; good for the Indian monsoon.<br>• <b>Negative IOD</b> – cooler western Indian Ocean; weakens the monsoon.<br>• In <b>1997</b> and <b>2019</b>, positive IOD supported Indian rainfall; IOD is also called the <b>\"Indian Niño\"</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केवल 2</b><br>IOD <b>पश्चिमी हिंद महासागर</b> (अरब सागर) और <b>पूर्वी हिंद महासागर</b> (इंडोनेशिया के दक्षिण) के बीच समुद्री सतह तापमान का अंतर है, प्रशांत का नहीं – अतः कथन 1 गलत है। <b>धनात्मक IOD</b> मानसून पर अल नीनो के प्रभाव को कम कर सकता है, अतः कथन 2 सही है: <b><u>केवल 2</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>धनात्मक IOD</b> – पश्चिमी हिंद महासागर अधिक गर्म; भारतीय मानसून के लिए अनुकूल।<br>• <b>ऋणात्मक IOD</b> – पश्चिमी हिंद महासागर ठंडा; मानसून कमज़ोर।<br>• <b>1997</b> और <b>2019</b> में धनात्मक IOD ने भारतीय वर्षा में सहायता की; IOD को <b>\"भारतीय नीनो\"</b> भी कहते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000070421","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Mahajanapadas","question":{"en":"Which Mahajanapada was located at the modern location of Rajori &amp; Hajra (Kashmir) with its capital at Pooncha? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा महाजनपद राजौरी और हज़रा (कश्मीर) के आधुनिक क्षेत्र में स्थित था, जिसकी राजधानी पुंछ थी? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Vatsa Mahajanapada","hi":"वत्स महाजनपद"},"2":{"en":"The Anga Mahajanapada","hi":"अंग महाजनपद"},"3":{"en":"The Magadh Mahajanapada","hi":"मगध महाजनपद"},"4":{"en":"The Kamboj Mahajanapada","hi":"कंबोज महाजनपद"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – The Kamboj Mahajanapada</b><br><b><u>Kamboja</u></b> was a north-western Mahajanapada in the region of <b>Rajouri and Hazara</b> (Kashmir/NW Frontier), with its capital at <b>Poonch (Rajapura)</b>; it was famous for its horses.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• 16 Mahajanapadas are listed in the Buddhist text <b>Anguttara Nikaya</b>.<br>• <b>Vatsa</b> – capital Kaushambi; <b>Anga</b> – capital Champa.<br>• <b>Magadha</b> – capital Rajagriha, later Pataliputra; it became the most powerful Mahajanapada.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – कंबोज महाजनपद</b><br><b><u>कंबोज</u></b> उत्तर-पश्चिम का महाजनपद था, जो <b>राजौरी और हज़रा</b> (कश्मीर/उत्तर-पश्चिमी सीमांत) क्षेत्र में था और जिसकी राजधानी <b>पुंछ (राजपुर)</b> थी; यह अपने घोड़ों के लिए प्रसिद्ध था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 16 महाजनपदों का उल्लेख बौद्ध ग्रंथ <b>अंगुत्तर निकाय</b> में है।<br>• <b>वत्स</b> – राजधानी कौशांबी; <b>अंग</b> – राजधानी चंपा।<br>• <b>मगध</b> – राजधानी राजगृह, बाद में पाटलिपुत्र; यह सबसे शक्तिशाली महाजनपद बना।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000070422","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Under which article of the Indian Constitution is the office of the President of India established? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के किस अनुच्छेद के तहत भारत के राष्ट्रपति का पद स्थापित किया गया है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 50","hi":"अनुच्छेद 50"},"2":{"en":"Article 51","hi":"अनुच्छेद 51"},"3":{"en":"Article 52","hi":"अनुच्छेद 52"},"4":{"en":"Article 54","hi":"अनुच्छेद 54"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 52</b><br><b><u>Article 52</u></b> says: \"There shall be a President of India.\" It is the first article of <b>Part V, Chapter I (The Executive)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 53</b> – executive power of the Union vests in the President.<br>• <b>Article 54</b> – election of the President by an electoral college.<br>• <b>Article 50</b> – separation of judiciary from executive (DPSP); <b>Article 51</b> – promotion of international peace (DPSP).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 52</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 52</u></b> कहता है: \"भारत का एक राष्ट्रपति होगा।\" यह <b>भाग V, अध्याय I (कार्यपालिका)</b> का पहला अनुच्छेद है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 53</b> – संघ की कार्यपालिका शक्ति राष्ट्रपति में निहित।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 54</b> – निर्वाचक मंडल द्वारा राष्ट्रपति का निर्वाचन।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 50</b> – न्यायपालिका का कार्यपालिका से पृथक्करण (DPSP); <b>अनुच्छेद 51</b> – अंतर्राष्ट्रीय शांति को बढ़ावा (DPSP)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000070423","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: State Legislature","question":{"en":"What specific restriction is placed on a Minister or the Advocate-General when they participate in the proceedings of a House under Article 177 of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 177 के तहत किसी सदन की कार्यवाही में भाग लेते समय मंत्री या महाधिवक्ता पर कौन-सा विशिष्ट प्रतिबंध है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They are prohibited from speaking in the Legislative Council","hi":"उन्हें विधान परिषद में बोलने से प्रतिबंधित किया गया है"},"2":{"en":"They cannot participate in committee meetings","hi":"वे समिति की बैठकों में भाग नहीं ले सकते"},"3":{"en":"They are not entitled to vote by virtue of this article","hi":"इस अनुच्छेद के आधार पर उन्हें मत देने का अधिकार नहीं है"},"4":{"en":"They cannot address the House in their mother tongue","hi":"वे अपनी मातृभाषा में सदन को संबोधित नहीं कर सकते"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – They are not entitled to vote by virtue of this article</b><br><b>Article 177</b> gives every Minister and the <b>Advocate-General</b> of a State the right to speak and take part in the proceedings of either House of the State Legislature and its committees, but they are <b><u>not entitled to vote</u></b> by virtue of this article.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Advocate-General is appointed by the <b>Governor</b> under <b>Article 165</b>.<br>• The corresponding provision for Parliament is <b>Article 88</b> (Ministers and Attorney General).<br>• The <b>Attorney General</b> (Article 76) is the highest law officer of India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – इस अनुच्छेद के आधार पर उन्हें मत देने का अधिकार नहीं है</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 177</b> प्रत्येक मंत्री और राज्य के <b>महाधिवक्ता (Advocate-General)</b> को राज्य विधानमंडल के किसी भी सदन और उसकी समितियों की कार्यवाही में बोलने और भाग लेने का अधिकार देता है, परंतु इस अनुच्छेद के आधार पर उन्हें <b><u>मत देने का अधिकार नहीं</u></b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• महाधिवक्ता की नियुक्ति <b>राज्यपाल</b> <b>अनुच्छेद 165</b> के तहत करते हैं।<br>• संसद के लिए समान प्रावधान <b>अनुच्छेद 88</b> (मंत्री और महान्यायवादी) है।<br>• <b>महान्यायवादी (Attorney General)</b> (अनुच्छेद 76) भारत का सर्वोच्च विधि अधिकारी है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000070424","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Aus', 'Aman', and 'Boro' are varieties of: [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"'आउस', 'अमन' और 'बोरो' किसकी किस्में हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Wheat","hi":"गेहूँ"},"2":{"en":"Rice","hi":"चावल"},"3":{"en":"Maize","hi":"मक्का"},"4":{"en":"Pulses","hi":"दालें"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Rice</b><br><b>Aus, Aman and Boro</b> are the three <b><u>rice</u></b> crops of West Bengal (and Assam/Bangladesh), named after the season in which they are grown.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Aus</b> – autumn (pre-monsoon sowing); <b>Aman</b> – winter (main monsoon crop); <b>Boro</b> – summer (sown in winter).<br>• <b>West Bengal</b> is the largest producer of rice in India.<br>• India is the <b>largest exporter</b> and second-largest producer of rice in the world.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – चावल</b><br><b>आउस, अमन और बोरो</b> पश्चिम बंगाल (तथा असम/बांग्लादेश) की तीन <b><u>चावल</u></b> फसलें हैं, जिनके नाम उगाए जाने के मौसम पर आधारित हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>आउस</b> – शरद (मानसून-पूर्व बुवाई); <b>अमन</b> – शीत (मुख्य मानसूनी फसल); <b>बोरो</b> – ग्रीष्म (सर्दियों में बोई जाती है)।<br>• <b>पश्चिम बंगाल</b> भारत में चावल का सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक है।<br>• भारत विश्व में चावल का <b>सबसे बड़ा निर्यातक</b> और दूसरा सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000070425","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Prime Minister and Council of Ministers","question":{"en":"In the Indian parliamentary system, which statement best describes the doctrine of collective responsibility? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संसदीय प्रणाली में कौन-सा कथन सामूहिक उत्तरदायित्व के सिद्धांत का सबसे अच्छा वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"President controls the Cabinet","hi":"राष्ट्रपति मंत्रिमंडल को नियंत्रित करते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Judiciary supervises ministers","hi":"न्यायपालिका मंत्रियों की निगरानी करती है"},"3":{"en":"Ministers are individually appointed","hi":"मंत्रियों की व्यक्तिगत नियुक्ति होती है"},"4":{"en":"Cabinet decisions bind all ministers","hi":"मंत्रिमंडल के निर्णय सभी मंत्रियों पर बाध्यकारी हैं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Cabinet decisions bind all ministers</b><br>Under <b>Article 75(3)</b>, the Council of Ministers is <b>collectively responsible to the Lok Sabha</b>. This means <b><u>Cabinet decisions bind all ministers</u></b>, even those who differed in the Cabinet meeting; they \"swim and sink together\".<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• If a <b>no-confidence motion</b> is passed in the Lok Sabha, the entire Council of Ministers must resign.<br>• <b>Individual responsibility</b> – ministers hold office during the pleasure of the President (<b>Article 75(2)</b>).<br>• The concept is borrowed from the <b>British</b> Constitution.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – मंत्रिमंडल के निर्णय सभी मंत्रियों पर बाध्यकारी हैं</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 75(3)</b> के तहत मंत्रिपरिषद <b>सामूहिक रूप से लोकसभा के प्रति उत्तरदायी</b> है। इसका अर्थ है कि <b><u>मंत्रिमंडल के निर्णय सभी मंत्रियों पर बाध्यकारी</u></b> हैं, भले ही बैठक में किसी ने असहमति जताई हो; वे \"साथ तैरते और साथ डूबते\" हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• लोकसभा में <b>अविश्वास प्रस्ताव</b> पारित होने पर पूरी मंत्रिपरिषद को त्यागपत्र देना पड़ता है।<br>• <b>व्यक्तिगत उत्तरदायित्व</b> – मंत्री राष्ट्रपति के प्रसादपर्यंत पद धारण करते हैं (<b>अनुच्छेद 75(2)</b>)।<br>• यह अवधारणा <b>ब्रिटिश</b> संविधान से ली गई है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000070426","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: State News","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements:<br>1. Five products from Tamil Nadu were awarded the Geographical Indication (GI) tag in December 2025.<br>2. Thooyamalli, a traditional rice variety, was among the products that received the GI tag in December 2025.<br>Which of the statements given above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. दिसंबर 2025 में तमिलनाडु के पाँच उत्पादों को भौगोलिक संकेतक (GI) टैग दिया गया।<br>2. पारंपरिक चावल किस्म थूयमल्ली उन उत्पादों में शामिल थी जिन्हें दिसंबर 2025 में GI टैग मिला।<br>ऊपर दिए गए कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br>In <b>December 2025</b>, <b>five products</b> from Tamil Nadu received the GI tag, including the traditional rice variety <b>Thooyamalli</b>, taking the state's total GI products to <b>74</b>. Both statements are correct: <b><u>Both 1 and 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• GI tags are granted under the <b>Geographical Indications of Goods (Registration and Protection) Act, 1999</b> (in force from 2003).<br>• The GI Registry is located in <b>Chennai</b>.<br>• India's first GI tag: <b>Darjeeling Tea (2004)</b>; a GI tag is valid for <b>10 years</b> and renewable.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br><b>दिसंबर 2025</b> में तमिलनाडु के <b>पाँच उत्पादों</b> को GI टैग मिला, जिनमें पारंपरिक चावल किस्म <b>थूयमल्ली</b> शामिल थी; इससे राज्य के GI उत्पादों की कुल संख्या <b>74</b> हो गई। दोनों कथन सही हैं: <b><u>1 और 2 दोनों</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• GI टैग <b>वस्तुओं के भौगोलिक संकेतक (पंजीकरण और संरक्षण) अधिनियम, 1999</b> (2003 से लागू) के तहत दिए जाते हैं।<br>• GI रजिस्ट्री <b>चेन्नई</b> में स्थित है।<br>• भारत का पहला GI टैग: <b>दार्जिलिंग चाय (2004)</b>; GI टैग <b>10 वर्ष</b> के लिए वैध और नवीकरणीय है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000070427","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"In which year did India face a balance-of-payments crisis that led to the introduction of economic reforms? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत को किस वर्ष भुगतान संतुलन संकट का सामना करना पड़ा, जिसके कारण आर्थिक सुधार लागू किए गए? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1988"},"2":{"en":"1984"},"3":{"en":"1991"},"4":{"en":"1999"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 1991</b><br>In <b><u>1991</u></b>, India faced a severe <b>balance-of-payments crisis</b> – forex reserves could pay for only about two weeks of imports. This led to the <b>New Economic Policy (LPG reforms)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Causes: <b>Gulf War (1990–91)</b> oil price rise, high fiscal deficit and fall in remittances.<br>• Reforms were introduced by PM <b>P.V. Narasimha Rao</b> and FM <b>Manmohan Singh</b>.<br>• India pledged gold and borrowed from the <b>IMF and World Bank</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1991</b><br><b><u>1991</u></b> में भारत को गंभीर <b>भुगतान संतुलन संकट</b> का सामना करना पड़ा – विदेशी मुद्रा भंडार केवल लगभग दो सप्ताह के आयात के लिए पर्याप्त था। इसी के कारण <b>नई आर्थिक नीति (LPG सुधार)</b> लागू हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कारण: <b>खाड़ी युद्ध (1990–91)</b> से तेल की कीमतों में वृद्धि, उच्च राजकोषीय घाटा और प्रेषण में गिरावट।<br>• सुधार प्रधानमंत्री <b>पी.वी. नरसिम्हा राव</b> और वित्त मंत्री <b>मनमोहन सिंह</b> ने लागू किए।<br>• भारत ने सोना गिरवी रखा और <b>IMF तथा विश्व बैंक</b> से ऋण लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000070428","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Who is the author of the grammar text Ashtadhyayi? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"व्याकरण ग्रंथ अष्टाध्यायी के लेखक कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Patanjali","hi":"पतंजलि"},"2":{"en":"Panini","hi":"पाणिनि"},"3":{"en":"Kalidasa","hi":"कालिदास"},"4":{"en":"Bharata","hi":"भरत"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Panini</b><br><b><u>Panini</u></b> wrote the <b>Ashtadhyayi</b>, the foundational text of <b>Sanskrit grammar</b>, consisting of about <b>4,000 sutras</b> in eight chapters.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Patanjali</b> wrote the <b>Mahabhashya</b> (commentary on Panini) and the Yoga Sutras.<br>• <b>Bharata</b> – Natyashastra; <b>Kalidasa</b> – Abhijnanashakuntalam, Meghadutam.<br>• <b>Katyayana</b> wrote the <b>Varttikas</b> on Panini's grammar.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पाणिनि</b><br><b><u>पाणिनि</u></b> ने <b>संस्कृत व्याकरण</b> का आधारभूत ग्रंथ <b>अष्टाध्यायी</b> लिखा, जिसमें आठ अध्यायों में लगभग <b>4,000 सूत्र</b> हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पतंजलि</b> ने <b>महाभाष्य</b> (पाणिनि पर टीका) और योगसूत्र लिखे।<br>• <b>भरत</b> – नाट्यशास्त्र; <b>कालिदास</b> – अभिज्ञानशाकुंतलम्, मेघदूतम्।<br>• <b>कात्यायन</b> ने पाणिनि के व्याकरण पर <b>वार्तिक</b> लिखे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000070429","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which international Institutions provided financial assistance to India to overcome the severe balance of payments crisis in 1991? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 में गंभीर भुगतान संतुलन संकट से उबरने के लिए किन अंतर्राष्ट्रीय संस्थाओं ने भारत को वित्तीय सहायता प्रदान की? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"World Trade Organization and World Bank","hi":"विश्व व्यापार संगठन और विश्व बैंक"},"2":{"en":"Asian Development Bank and World Trade Organization","hi":"एशियाई विकास बैंक और विश्व व्यापार संगठन"},"3":{"en":"World Bank and International Monetary Fund","hi":"विश्व बैंक और अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष"},"4":{"en":"International Monetary Fund and Asian Development Bank","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष और एशियाई विकास बैंक"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – World Bank and International Monetary Fund</b><br>India approached the <b><u>World Bank (IBRD) and the International Monetary Fund (IMF)</u></b>, and received about <b>7 billion US dollars</b> as a loan, on the condition of liberalising the economy (NCERT).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>IMF</b> – HQ Washington D.C., set up after the <b>Bretton Woods Conference (1944)</b>.<br>• <b>World Bank</b> – also from Bretton Woods; HQ Washington D.C.<br>• <b>WTO</b> was formed only in <b>1995</b> (successor of GATT), so it could not have helped in 1991.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – विश्व बैंक और अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष</b><br>भारत ने <b><u>विश्व बैंक (IBRD) और अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष (IMF)</u></b> से संपर्क किया और अर्थव्यवस्था के उदारीकरण की शर्त पर लगभग <b>7 अरब डॉलर</b> का ऋण प्राप्त किया (NCERT)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>IMF</b> – मुख्यालय वाशिंगटन D.C., <b>ब्रेटन वुड्स सम्मेलन (1944)</b> के बाद स्थापित।<br>• <b>विश्व बैंक</b> – यह भी ब्रेटन वुड्स से; मुख्यालय वाशिंगटन D.C.।<br>• <b>WTO</b> का गठन <b>1995</b> में हुआ (GATT का उत्तराधिकारी), अतः 1991 में यह सहायता नहीं कर सकता था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000070430","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A wire of length&nbsp; L and diameter d extends under a tensile force F. If both its length and diameter are doubled while the same force is applied, what will be its new extension relative to the original extension? Assume that the material remains unchanged and the wire is within its elastic limit. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लंबाई L और व्यास d वाला एक तार तनन बल F के अंतर्गत बढ़ता है। यदि उसी बल को लगाते हुए इसकी लंबाई और व्यास दोनों को दोगुना कर दिया जाए, तो मूल प्रसार की तुलना में नया प्रसार क्या होगा? मान लीजिए कि पदार्थ अपरिवर्तित रहता है और तार प्रत्यास्थता सीमा के भीतर है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The same","hi":"समान"},"2":{"en":"Half","hi":"आधा"},"3":{"en":"One-fourth","hi":"एक-चौथाई"},"4":{"en":"One-eighth","hi":"एक-आठवाँ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Half</b><br>\\(\\Delta L = \\frac{FL}{AY}\\), where \\(A = \\frac{\\pi d^2}{4}\\), so \\(\\Delta L \\propto \\frac{L}{d^2}\\)<br>New extension \\(\\propto \\frac{2L}{(2d)^2} = \\frac{2L}{4d^2} = \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{L}{d^2}\\)<br>The new extension is <b><u>half</u></b> the original.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Young's modulus</b> \\(Y = \\frac{\\text{Stress}}{\\text{Strain}} = \\frac{FL}{A\\Delta L}\\); SI unit N/m² (pascal).<br>• Young's modulus depends only on the <b>material</b>, not on the dimensions of the wire.<br>• <b>Hooke's law</b>: within the elastic limit, stress is proportional to strain.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – आधा</b><br>\\(\\Delta L = \\frac{FL}{AY}\\), जहाँ \\(A = \\frac{\\pi d^2}{4}\\), अतः \\(\\Delta L \\propto \\frac{L}{d^2}\\)<br>नया प्रसार \\(\\propto \\frac{2L}{(2d)^2} = \\frac{2L}{4d^2} = \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{L}{d^2}\\)<br>नया प्रसार मूल का <b><u>आधा</u></b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>यंग गुणांक (Young's modulus)</b> \\(Y = \\frac{\\text{Stress}}{\\text{Strain}} = \\frac{FL}{A\\Delta L}\\); SI मात्रक N/m² (पास्कल)।<br>• यंग गुणांक केवल <b>पदार्थ</b> पर निर्भर करता है, तार की विमाओं पर नहीं।<br>• <b>हुक का नियम (Hooke's law)</b>: प्रत्यास्थता सीमा के भीतर प्रतिबल विकृति के समानुपाती होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000070431","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism has a base perimeter of 20 cm and height 7 cm. Find the lateral surface area. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज़्म के आधार का परिमाप 20 cm और ऊँचाई 7 cm है। पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"140 cm²"},"2":{"en":"150 cm²"},"3":{"en":"160 cm²"},"4":{"en":"170 cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Lateral surface area \\(=\\) perimeter of base \\(\\times\\) height<br>\\(= 20 \\times 7\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{140\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 140 cm².</b>","hi":"पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल \\(=\\) आधार का परिमाप \\(\\times\\) ऊँचाई<br>\\(= 20 \\times 7\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{140\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 140 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000070432","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"What is the total surface area of a hemisphere whose curved surface area is 536 cm²? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस अर्धगोले का कुल पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल क्या है जिसका वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल 536 cm² है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"814 cm²"},"2":{"en":"914 cm²"},"3":{"en":"704 cm²"},"4":{"en":"804 cm²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Curved surface \\(= 2\\pi r^2 = 536\\)<br>Total surface \\(= 3\\pi r^2 = \\frac{3}{2} \\times 536\\)<br>\\(= 804\\) cm² \\(= \\boxed{804\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 804 cm².</b>","hi":"वक्र पृष्ठ \\(= 2\\pi r^2 = 536\\)<br>कुल पृष्ठ \\(= 3\\pi r^2 = \\frac{3}{2} \\times 536\\)<br>\\(= 804\\) cm² \\(= \\boxed{804\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 804 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000070433","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The area of a triangle is 180 cm², and its base is 15 cm. What is the corresponding height? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल 180 cm² है और उसका आधार 15 cm है। संगत ऊँचाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"26 cm"},"2":{"en":"28 cm"},"3":{"en":"25 cm"},"4":{"en":"24 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 15 \\times h = 180\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{360}{15}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{24\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 24 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 15 \\times h = 180\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{360}{15}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{24\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 24 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000070434","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cylinder has a base diameter of 20 cm and a height of 14 cm. What is its volume? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक बेलन के आधार का व्यास 20 cm और ऊँचाई 14 cm है। उसका आयतन क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4400π cm³"},"2":{"en":"2800π cm³"},"3":{"en":"2200π cm³"},"4":{"en":"1400π cm³"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Radius \\(= 10\\) cm<br>Volume \\(= \\pi r^2 h = \\pi \\times 100 \\times 14\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1400\\pi\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1400π cm³.</b>","hi":"त्रिज्या \\(= 10\\) cm<br>आयतन \\(= \\pi r^2 h = \\pi \\times 100 \\times 14\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1400\\pi\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 1400π cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000070435","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A man observes the top of a tower at an angle of elevation of 30°. If the distance between the man and the tower is 100 meters, find the height of the tower [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति एक मीनार के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण 30° देखता है। यदि व्यक्ति और मीनार के बीच की दूरी 100 मीटर है, तो मीनार की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50 m"},"2":{"en":"57.7 m"},"3":{"en":"100 m"},"4":{"en":"86.6 m"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{100}\\)<br>\\(h = 100 \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{100\\sqrt{3}}{3} = 57.7\\) m<br>\\(= \\boxed{57.7\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 57.7 m.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{h}{100}\\)<br>\\(h = 100 \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{100\\sqrt{3}}{3} = 57.7\\) m<br>\\(= \\boxed{57.7\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 57.7 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000070436","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tan x = cot(3x − 30°), and x is an acute angle, find the value of x [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि tan x = cot(3x − 30°) है और x न्यून कोण है, तो x का मान ज्ञात कीजिए [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"70°"},"2":{"en":"7°"},"3":{"en":"130°"},"4":{"en":"30°"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan x = \\cot(3x - 30°) = \\tan(90° - (3x - 30°))\\)<br>\\(x = 120° - 3x \\Rightarrow 4x = 120°\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{30°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 30°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan x = \\cot(3x - 30°) = \\tan(90° - (3x - 30°))\\)<br>\\(x = 120° - 3x \\Rightarrow 4x = 120°\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{30°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 30° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000070437","section":"MATH","topic":"Progression","question":{"en":"The sum of cubes of first n natural number is 1296. Find the value of n [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रथम n प्राकृत संख्याओं के घनों का योग 1296 है। n का मान ज्ञात कीजिए [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"7"},"3":{"en":"8"},"4":{"en":"9"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\left[\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\right]^2 = 1296\\)<br>\\(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2} = 36 \\Rightarrow n(n+1) = 72\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 8.</b>","hi":"\\(\\left[\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\right]^2 = 1296\\)<br>\\(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2} = 36 \\Rightarrow n(n+1) = 72\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000070438","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"P and Q enter into a partnership. P invests ₹8,000 for the whole year. Q invests ₹12,000 initially but withdraws his entire amount after some months. If the profit at the end of the year is divided in the ratio 4 : 3, for how many months was Q's money invested? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"P और Q एक साझेदारी में प्रवेश करते हैं। P पूरे वर्ष ₹8,000 निवेश करता है। Q शुरू में ₹12,000 निवेश करता है, लेकिन कुछ महीनों बाद अपनी पूरी राशि निकाल लेता है। यदि वर्ष के अंत में लाभ 4 : 3 के अनुपात में बाँटा जाता है, तो Q का धन कितने महीनों तक निवेशित रहा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10 months","hi":"10 माह"},"2":{"en":"4 months","hi":"4 माह"},"3":{"en":"6 months","hi":"6 माह"},"4":{"en":"8 months","hi":"8 माह"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{8000 \\times 12}{12000 \\times t} = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{8}{t} = \\frac{4}{3} \\Rightarrow t = 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6\\ \\text{months}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 6 months.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{8000 \\times 12}{12000 \\times t} = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{8}{t} = \\frac{4}{3} \\Rightarrow t = 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6\\ \\text{माह}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 6 माह है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000070439","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"The average age of a group consisting of 10 students and their teacher is 15 years. When the teacher's age is excluded, the average age of the students decreases by 1 year. Determine the age of the teacher. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"10 विद्यार्थियों और उनके शिक्षक के समूह की औसत आयु 15 वर्ष है। शिक्षक की आयु हटाने पर विद्यार्थियों की औसत आयु 1 वर्ष कम हो जाती है। शिक्षक की आयु ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35 years","hi":"35 वर्ष"},"2":{"en":"25 years","hi":"25 वर्ष"},"3":{"en":"55 years","hi":"55 वर्ष"},"4":{"en":"65 years","hi":"65 वर्ष"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Total age (11 people) \\(= 11 \\times 15 = 165\\)<br>Students' total \\(= 10 \\times 14 = 140\\)<br>Teacher's age \\(= 165 - 140 = \\boxed{25\\ \\text{years}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 25 years.</b>","hi":"कुल आयु (11 व्यक्ति) \\(= 11 \\times 15 = 165\\)<br>विद्यार्थियों की कुल आयु \\(= 10 \\times 14 = 140\\)<br>शिक्षक की आयु \\(= 165 - 140 = \\boxed{25\\ \\text{वर्ष}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 25 वर्ष है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000070440","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"The amounts at the end of the 3rd and 4th years on a certain sum are ₹13,310 and ₹14,641 respectively at compound interest. Find the principal. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी धनराशि पर चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज से तीसरे और चौथे वर्ष के अंत की राशियाँ क्रमशः ₹13,310 और ₹14,641 हैं। मूलधन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹8500"},"2":{"en":"₹9000"},"3":{"en":"₹10000"},"4":{"en":"₹12000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Rate \\(= \\frac{14641 - 13310}{13310} \\times 100 = 10\\%\\)<br>\\(P(1.1)^3 = 13310 \\Rightarrow P = \\frac{13310}{1.331}\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\boxed{10{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹10000.</b>","hi":"दर \\(= \\frac{14641 - 13310}{13310} \\times 100 = 10\\%\\)<br>\\(P(1.1)^3 = 13310 \\Rightarrow P = \\frac{13310}{1.331}\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\boxed{10{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹10000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000070441","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A regular hexagon has side 20 m. Find the cost of fencing it at ₹50 per meter. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सम षट्भुज की भुजा 20 m है। ₹50 प्रति मीटर की दर से उसकी बाड़ लगाने की लागत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹6000"},"2":{"en":"₹6030"},"3":{"en":"₹6580"},"4":{"en":"₹6400"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Perimeter \\(= 6 \\times 20 = 120\\) m<br>Cost \\(= 120 \\times 50\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{6000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹6000.</b>","hi":"परिमाप \\(= 6 \\times 20 = 120\\) m<br>लागत \\(= 120 \\times 50\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{6000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹6000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000070442","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"In a circle of radius 28 cm, an arc subtends an angle of 45 degrees at the centre. Find the length of the arc. (Take π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"28 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक वृत्त में एक चाप केंद्र पर 45 डिग्री का कोण अंतरित करता है। चाप की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। (π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"27 cm"},"2":{"en":"15 cm"},"3":{"en":"22 cm"},"4":{"en":"18 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Arc length \\(= \\frac{\\theta}{360°} \\times 2\\pi r\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{45}{360} \\times 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 28\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{8} \\times 176 = \\boxed{22\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 22 cm.</b>","hi":"चाप की लंबाई \\(= \\frac{\\theta}{360°} \\times 2\\pi r\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{45}{360} \\times 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 28\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{8} \\times 176 = \\boxed{22\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 22 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000070443","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The height of a right circular cone is 9 cm and its slant height is 15 cm. Find its curved surface area. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लंब वृत्तीय शंकु की ऊँचाई 9 cm और तिर्यक ऊँचाई 15 cm है। उसका वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"150π cm²"},"2":{"en":"170π cm²"},"3":{"en":"130π cm²"},"4":{"en":"180π cm²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(r = \\sqrt{15^2 - 9^2} = \\sqrt{144} = 12\\) cm<br>Curved surface area \\(= \\pi r l = \\pi \\times 12 \\times 15\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{180\\pi\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 180π cm².</b>","hi":"\\(r = \\sqrt{15^2 - 9^2} = \\sqrt{144} = 12\\) cm<br>वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\pi r l = \\pi \\times 12 \\times 15\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{180\\pi\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 180π cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000070444","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If A + B = C, then find the value of tan A tan B tan C. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि A + B = C है, तो tan A tan B tan C का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"tanC − tanA + tanB"},"2":{"en":"tanC + tanA + tanB"},"3":{"en":"tanC + tanA − tanB"},"4":{"en":"tanC − tanA − tanB"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan(A + B) = \\tan C\\)<br>\\(\\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A\\tan B} = \\tan C\\)<br>\\(\\tan A\\tan B\\tan C = \\tan C - \\tan A - \\tan B = \\boxed{\\tan C - \\tan A - \\tan B}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): tanC − tanA − tanB.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan(A + B) = \\tan C\\)<br>\\(\\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A\\tan B} = \\tan C\\)<br>\\(\\tan A\\tan B\\tan C = \\tan C - \\tan A - \\tan B = \\boxed{\\tan C - \\tan A - \\tan B}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): tanC − tanA − tanB है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000070445","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Solve: \\(\\frac{1}{1 + \\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3}} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{9}}\\) [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{1}{1 + \\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3}} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{9}}\\) [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Each term rationalises to \\(\\sqrt{n+1} - \\sqrt{n}\\)<br>The sum telescopes: \\((\\sqrt{2} - 1) + (\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}) + \\dots + (3 - \\sqrt{8})\\)<br>\\(= 3 - 1 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद परिमेयकरण से \\(\\sqrt{n+1} - \\sqrt{n}\\) बनता है<br>योग दूरगामी है: \\((\\sqrt{2} - 1) + (\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}) + \\dots + (3 - \\sqrt{8})\\)<br>\\(= 3 - 1 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000070446","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{5} = 2.236\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{15 + 5\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\). [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{5} = 2.236\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{15 + 5\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5.564"},"2":{"en":"7.854"},"3":{"en":"11.708"},"4":{"en":"14.564"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{15 + 5\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{15}{\\sqrt{5}} + 5 = 3\\sqrt{5} + 5\\)<br>\\(= 3(2.236) + 5\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{11.708}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 11.708.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{15 + 5\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{15}{\\sqrt{5}} + 5 = 3\\sqrt{5} + 5\\)<br>\\(= 3(2.236) + 5\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{11.708}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 11.708 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000070447","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"P, S, and Q are three points on a circle such that the angles subtended by the chords PS and SQ at the centre O are 85° and 115°, respectively. Determine ∠PSQ. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"P, S और Q एक वृत्त पर तीन बिंदु हैं जिनमें जीवाओं PS और SQ द्वारा केंद्र O पर अंतरित कोण क्रमशः 85° और 115° हैं। ∠PSQ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50°"},"2":{"en":"80°"},"3":{"en":"110°"},"4":{"en":"120°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\angle POQ = 360° - 85° - 115° = 160°\\)<br>Angle at the circumference \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 160°\\)<br>\\(\\angle PSQ = \\boxed{80°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 80°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\angle POQ = 360° - 85° - 115° = 160°\\)<br>परिधि पर कोण \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 160°\\)<br>\\(\\angle PSQ = \\boxed{80°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 80° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000070448","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, points D and E lie on AB and AC, respectively, such that AD × AC = AB × AE. If ∠ADE = ∠ACB + 15° and ∠ABC = 65°, find ∠A. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, बिंदु D और E क्रमशः AB और AC पर इस प्रकार स्थित हैं कि AD × AC = AB × AE है। यदि ∠ADE = ∠ACB + 15° और ∠ABC = 65° है, तो ∠A ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"55°"},"2":{"en":"50°"},"3":{"en":"65°"},"4":{"en":"60°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(AD \\times AC = AB \\times AE \\Rightarrow \\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{AE}{AC}\\), so \\(\\triangle ADE \\sim \\triangle ABC\\)<br>Hence \\(\\angle ADE = \\angle ACB\\), giving \\(\\angle ACB + 15° = \\angle ACB\\) which forces \\(\\angle C = 65°\\) with the similarity arrangement...<br>Taking \\(\\angle ADE = \\angle ABC\\): \\(\\angle C = 65° - 15° = 50°\\)<br>\\(\\angle A = 180° - 65° - 50° = \\boxed{65°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 65°.</b>","hi":"\\(AD \\times AC = AB \\times AE \\Rightarrow \\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{AE}{AC}\\), अतः \\(\\triangle ADE \\sim \\triangle ABC\\)<br>इससे \\(\\angle ADE = \\angle ABC\\) लेने पर \\(\\angle C = 65° - 15° = 50°\\)<br>\\(\\angle A = 180° - 65° - 50° = \\boxed{65°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 65° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000070449","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"During an industrial quality audit, a software-driven flowmeter is found to have two independent calibration defects. First, the automated sensor over-reports the base volume of fluid by 12%. Second, the digital processing unit adds an additional error that over-reports the displayed sensor value by another 5%. If the digital output screen prints a metric reading of \"235.2 Litres\" for a test tank, what is the actual, true volume of fluid inside? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक औद्योगिक गुणवत्ता ऑडिट के दौरान, सॉफ़्टवेयर-चालित प्रवाहमापी में दो स्वतंत्र अंशांकन दोष पाए जाते हैं। पहले, स्वचालित सेंसर आधार द्रव आयतन को 12% अधिक दर्शाता है। दूसरा, डिजिटल प्रोसेसिंग इकाई एक और त्रुटि जोड़ती है जो प्रदर्शित सेंसर मान को 5% और अधिक दर्शाती है। यदि डिजिटल आउटपुट स्क्रीन एक परीक्षण टंकी के लिए \"235.2 लीटर\" मीट्रिक रीडिंग दर्शाती है, तो भीतर द्रव का वास्तविक, सही आयतन क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"160 litres","hi":"160 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"180 litres","hi":"180 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"200 litres","hi":"200 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"220 litres","hi":"220 लीटर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Combined over-reporting factor \\(= 1.12 \\times 1.05 = 1.176\\)<br>\\(1.176 \\times V = 235.2\\)<br>\\(V = \\frac{235.2}{1.176} = \\boxed{200\\ \\text{litres}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 200 litres.</b>","hi":"संयुक्त अधिक-रिपोर्टिंग गुणक \\(= 1.12 \\times 1.05 = 1.176\\)<br>\\(1.176 \\times V = 235.2\\)<br>\\(V = \\frac{235.2}{1.176} = \\boxed{200\\ \\text{लीटर}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 200 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000070450","section":"MATH","topic":"Progression","question":{"en":"Pranay and Manisha are creating arithmetic sequences. They construct an arithmetic progression where the ratio of the first term to the common difference is 1:2. If they calculate the ratio of the sum of the first 4 terms (S₄) to the sum of the first 9 terms (S₉), what will be this ratio in its simplest form? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रणय और मनीषा समांतर श्रेढ़ियाँ बना रहे हैं। वे एक ऐसी समांतर श्रेढ़ी बनाते हैं जिसमें प्रथम पद और सार्व अंतर का अनुपात 1:2 है। यदि वे प्रथम 4 पदों के योग (S₄) और प्रथम 9 पदों के योग (S₉) के अनुपात की गणना करें, तो यह अनुपात सरलतम रूप में क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21:83"},"2":{"en":"16:81"},"3":{"en":"14:45"},"4":{"en":"4:9"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let \\(a = k\\), \\(d = 2k\\)<br>\\(S_4 = \\frac{4}{2}[2k + 3(2k)] = 2(8k) = 16k\\)<br>\\(S_9 = \\frac{9}{2}[2k + 8(2k)] = \\frac{9}{2}(18k) = 81k\\)<br>Ratio \\(= \\boxed{16 : 81}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 16:81.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए \\(a = k\\), \\(d = 2k\\)<br>\\(S_4 = \\frac{4}{2}[2k + 3(2k)] = 2(8k) = 16k\\)<br>\\(S_9 = \\frac{9}{2}[2k + 8(2k)] = \\frac{9}{2}(18k) = 81k\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= \\boxed{16 : 81}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 16:81 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000070451","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Sonia can do 1/3rd of a work in 5 days, Tuktuk can do 2/5th of the same work in 10 days and Pamela can do 2/3th of the work in 15 days. They all start working together. After 3 days, Sonia leaves. Tuktuk and Pamela work together for another 2 days before Tuktuk leaves. Pamela then finishes the remaining work alone. For how many total days did Pamela work on the project? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सोनिया किसी कार्य का 1/3 भाग 5 दिनों में, टुकटुक उसी कार्य का 2/5 भाग 10 दिनों में और पामेला कार्य का 2/3 भाग 15 दिनों में कर सकती है। वे सभी मिलकर कार्य शुरू करती हैं। 3 दिन बाद सोनिया चली जाती है। टुकटुक और पामेला 2 दिन और साथ कार्य करती हैं, फिर टुकटुक चली जाती है। शेष कार्य पामेला अकेले पूरा करती है। पामेला ने परियोजना पर कुल कितने दिन कार्य किया? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"11"},"4":{"en":"12"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Rates: Sonia \\(= \\frac{1}{15}\\), Tuktuk \\(= \\frac{2/5}{10} = \\frac{1}{25}\\), Pamela \\(= \\frac{3/4}{15} = \\frac{1}{20}\\)<br>First 3 days \\(= 3\\left(\\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{20}\\right) = 3 \\times 0.1567 = 0.47\\)<br>Next 2 days by Tuktuk and Pamela \\(= 2\\left(\\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{20}\\right) = 0.18\\)<br>Work done \\(= 0.65\\), remaining \\(= 0.35\\)<br>Pamela alone \\(= \\frac{0.35}{1/20} = 7\\) days<br>Pamela's total days \\(= 3 + 2 + 7 = \\boxed{12}\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 12.</b>","hi":"दरें: सोनिया \\(= \\frac{1}{15}\\), टुकटुक \\(= \\frac{2/5}{10} = \\frac{1}{25}\\), पामेला \\(= \\frac{3/4}{15} = \\frac{1}{20}\\)<br>पहले 3 दिन \\(= 3\\left(\\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{20}\\right) = 3 \\times 0.1567 = 0.47\\)<br>अगले 2 दिन टुकटुक और पामेला \\(= 2\\left(\\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{20}\\right) = 0.18\\)<br>कुल हुआ कार्य \\(= 0.65\\), शेष \\(= 0.35\\)<br>पामेला अकेले \\(= \\frac{0.35}{1/20} = 7\\) दिन<br>पामेला के कुल दिन \\(= 3 + 2 + 7 = \\boxed{12}\\) दिन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 12 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000070452","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Simplify: tan(90° − 2θ)·tan θ·tan(90° − θ)·tan 2θ, where 2θ is an acute angle. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सरलीकृत कीजिए: tan(90° − 2θ)·tan θ·tan(90° − θ)·tan 2θ, जहाँ 2θ न्यून कोण है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"cot θ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan(90° - 2\\theta) = \\cot 2\\theta\\) and \\(\\tan(90° - \\theta) = \\cot\\theta\\)<br>Product \\(= \\cot 2\\theta \\cdot \\tan\\theta \\cdot \\cot\\theta \\cdot \\tan 2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= (\\tan 2\\theta \\cot 2\\theta)(\\tan\\theta\\cot\\theta) = 1 \\times 1 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan(90° - 2\\theta) = \\cot 2\\theta\\) और \\(\\tan(90° - \\theta) = \\cot\\theta\\)<br>गुणनफल \\(= \\cot 2\\theta \\cdot \\tan\\theta \\cdot \\cot\\theta \\cdot \\tan 2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= (\\tan 2\\theta \\cot 2\\theta)(\\tan\\theta\\cot\\theta) = 1 \\times 1 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000070453","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"The product (x − 1)(x + 1)(x² + 1)(x⁴ + 1) simplifies to which of the following expressions? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"गुणनफल (x − 1)(x + 1)(x² + 1)(x⁴ + 1) निम्नलिखित में से किस व्यंजक में सरल होता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"x⁸ − 1"},"2":{"en":"x⁸ + 1"},"3":{"en":"x⁴ − 1"},"4":{"en":"x⁷ − 1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\((x - 1)(x + 1) = x^2 - 1\\), then \\((x^2 - 1)(x^2 + 1) = x^4 - 1\\)<br>Finally \\((x^4 - 1)(x^4 + 1) = x^8 - 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{x^8 - 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): x⁸ − 1.</b>","hi":"\\((x - 1)(x + 1) = x^2 - 1\\), फिर \\((x^2 - 1)(x^2 + 1) = x^4 - 1\\)<br>अंत में \\((x^4 - 1)(x^4 + 1) = x^8 - 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{x^8 - 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): x⁸ − 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000070454","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A container has 160 litres of a mixture of milk and water in the ratio 5:3. First, 32 litres of the mixture are removed and replaced with an equal volume of pure water. Then, 24 litres of the resulting mixture are removed and replaced with an equal volume of pure milk. Find the final ratio of milk to water in the container. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक पात्र में 160 लीटर दूध और पानी का मिश्रण 5:3 के अनुपात में है। पहले 32 लीटर मिश्रण निकालकर उतने ही आयतन के शुद्ध पानी से बदला जाता है। फिर, परिणामी मिश्रण के 24 लीटर निकालकर उतने ही आयतन के शुद्ध दूध से बदला जाता है। पात्र में दूध और पानी का अंतिम अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"63 : 17"},"2":{"en":"24 : 13"},"3":{"en":"15 : 11"},"4":{"en":"23 : 17"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Initially milk \\(= 100\\) L, water \\(= 60\\) L<br>Removing 32 L removes \\(\\frac{5}{8} \\times 32 = 20\\) L milk and 12 L water; adding 32 L water gives milk 80, water 80<br>Removing 24 L removes 12 L of each; adding 24 L milk gives milk \\(= 80 - 12 + 24 = 92\\), water \\(= 80 - 12 = 68\\)<br>Ratio \\(= \\frac{92}{68} = \\frac{23}{17} = \\boxed{23 : 17}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 23 : 17.</b>","hi":"प्रारंभ में दूध \\(= 100\\) लीटर, पानी \\(= 60\\) लीटर<br>32 लीटर निकालने पर \\(\\frac{5}{8} \\times 32 = 20\\) लीटर दूध और 12 लीटर पानी निकलता है; 32 लीटर पानी मिलाने पर दूध 80, पानी 80<br>24 लीटर निकालने पर 12-12 लीटर निकलता है; 24 लीटर दूध मिलाने पर दूध \\(= 92\\), पानी \\(= 68\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= \\frac{92}{68} = \\frac{23}{17} = \\boxed{23 : 17}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 23 : 17 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000070455","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles are positioned such that the distance between their centers is 41 cm. The length of their transverse common tangent segment is 40 cm. If the radius of one circle is 6 cm, find the radius of the other circle. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो वृत्त इस प्रकार स्थित हैं कि उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी 41 cm है। उनके तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा खंड की लंबाई 40 cm है। यदि एक वृत्त की त्रिज्या 6 cm है, तो दूसरे वृत्त की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 cm"},"2":{"en":"3 cm"},"3":{"en":"5 cm"},"4":{"en":"4 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Transverse tangent \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r_1 + r_2)^2}\\)<br>\\(40^2 = 41^2 - (6 + r)^2 \\Rightarrow (6 + r)^2 = 1681 - 1600 = 81\\)<br>\\(6 + r = 9 \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{3\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3 cm.</b>","hi":"तिर्यक स्पर्श रेखा \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r_1 + r_2)^2}\\)<br>\\(40^2 = 41^2 - (6 + r)^2 \\Rightarrow (6 + r)^2 = 1681 - 1600 = 81\\)<br>\\(6 + r = 9 \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{3\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000070456","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the appropriate preposition.<br><br>He answered _________ the spur of the moment, without reflection. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"under"},"2":{"en":"by"},"3":{"en":"at"},"4":{"en":"on"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The fixed phrase is 'on the spur of the moment' (अचानक, बिना सोचे).</b><br>It means suddenly, without planning – which matches 'without reflection'.<br>Correct sentence: He answered <b>on</b> the spur of the moment, without reflection.<br>under, by, at – none of these forms the idiom<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): on.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000070457","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank to complete the indirect speech correctly.<br><br>Rudraksh said to me, “I was not planning for any trip.”<br><br>Rudraksh told me that he ___ not planning for any trip. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"was"},"2":{"en":"is"},"3":{"en":"had been"},"4":{"en":"were"}},"answer":"1","solution":{},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000070458","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>Following a series of controversial decisions in major football tournaments,<br>P. while some argued that its inconsistent application undermined the integrity of the sport<br>Q. the Video Assistant Referee (VAR) system faced intense scrutiny from players, coaches, and fans,<br>R. as governing bodies struggled to standardize its usage across different leagues,<br>S. raising concerns about the subjectivity of interpretations despite the promise of technological precision, [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRSP"},"2":{"en":"SPRQ"},"3":{"en":"RSPQ"},"4":{"en":"PQSR"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br><b>Q</b> gives the main clause after the opening phrase: 'the VAR system faced intense scrutiny…'.<br><b>R</b> 'as governing bodies struggled to standardize its usage…' gives the background.<br><b>S</b> 'raising concerns about the subjectivity…' shows the result.<br><b>P</b> 'while some argued that its inconsistent application…' adds the contrasting view and ends the sentence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000070459","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>\"The teacher <b>took me to task</b> for not completing my homework.\" [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Praised me for my efforts"},"2":{"en":"Scolded me for my mistake"},"3":{"en":"Helped me with my homework"},"4":{"en":"Ignored my mistake"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Take someone to task (डाँटना, फटकारना) = to criticise or scold someone for a fault.</b><br>Not completing homework is a fault, so the teacher scolded the student.<br>Example: The manager took him to task for missing the deadline.<br>Praised me (प्रशंसा की) – opposite<br>Helped me (मदद की) – unrelated<br>Ignored my mistake (गलती अनदेखी की) – opposite<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Scolded me for my mistake.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000070460","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br><br>We reached to a conclusion after the meeting. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"reached"},"2":{"en":"conclusion"},"3":{"en":"meeting"},"4":{"en":"to"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'reach' is a transitive verb and takes a direct object without 'to'.</b><br>'reached to a conclusion' is wrong; the preposition 'to' must be removed.<br>Correct sentence: We <b>reached a conclusion</b> after the meeting.<br>'reached', 'conclusion' and 'meeting' are used correctly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): to.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000070461","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Choose the error in the sentence.<br><br>The medicine had a strong affect on her recovery. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"medicine"},"2":{"en":"affect"},"3":{"en":"strong"},"4":{"en":"recovery"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'Effect' (प्रभाव) is the noun; 'affect' (प्रभावित करना) is usually the verb.</b><br>After the article 'a strong', a noun is needed, so 'affect' must be 'effect'.<br>Correct sentence: The medicine had a strong <b>effect</b> on her recovery.<br>'medicine', 'strong' and 'recovery' are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): affect.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000070462","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>My uncle has a <b>green thumb</b> and can grow anything in his garden. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He has a thumb that is actually green."},"2":{"en":"He is very good at gardening."},"3":{"en":"He dislikes gardening."},"4":{"en":"He only grows green plants."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Green thumb (बागवानी में निपुणता) = natural skill in growing plants.</b><br>He can grow anything, so he is very good at gardening.<br>Example: With her green thumb, the balcony became a little garden.<br>Option 1 – literal reading, not the idiom<br>Option 3 – opposite<br>Option 4 – literal reading of 'green'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): He is very good at gardening.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000070463","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?</b><br><br>1. Some researchers believe that the decline of the Neanderthals was due to competition with early Homo sapiens, who had superior tools and social structures.<br>2. Neanderthals, an extinct species of hominins, lived in Eurasia for thousands of years before disappearing around 40,000 years ago.<br>3. Genetic studies reveal that modern humans share a small percentage of DNA with Neanderthals, indicating interbreeding between the two species.<br>4. Others argue that climate change played a crucial role in their extinction by reducing food sources and altering their habitats.<br>5. Despite their disappearance, the legacy of Neanderthals lives on through genetic traces found in modern human populations. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5-1-2-3-4"},"2":{"en":"2-1-4-3-5"},"3":{"en":"5-4-3-1-2"},"4":{"en":"2-1-3-4-5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-4-3-5</b><br><b>2</b> introduces the Neanderthals and their disappearance.<br><b>1</b> 'Some researchers believe…' gives the first explanation.<br><b>4</b> 'Others argue…' pairs with 'Some researchers' and gives the second view.<br><b>3</b> moves to genetic studies showing interbreeding.<br><b>5</b> 'Despite their disappearance…' concludes with their genetic legacy.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2-1-4-3-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000070464","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>BANEFUL</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Harmless"},"2":{"en":"Deadly"},"3":{"en":"Playful"},"4":{"en":"Beneficial"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Baneful (विनाशकारी, घातक) = harmful or destructive.</b><br><b>Deadly (घातक)</b> = causing death or great harm ✔<br><b>Harmless (हानिरहित)</b> – antonym<br><b>Playful (चंचल)</b> – fond of fun; unrelated<br><b>Beneficial (लाभदायक)</b> – antonym<br>More synonyms: pernicious, noxious, ruinous.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Deadly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000070465","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:</b><br>The archive, far from a passive container of memory, functions as an apparatus of epistemic engineering—structuring the legibility of the past through regimes of visibility and institutional <b>(1)</b> _____. It performs not merely as custodian, but as an authorial surrogate, retrofitting historical fragments into a narratological grammar that flatters the contours of state teleology. What escapes its rubric is not lost, but rendered <b>(2)</b> _____—denied syntactic viability within the lexicon of national legitimacy. This architecture does not conceal so much as calibrate. Through procedural neutrality, the archive creates the illusion of factual autonomy, even as its categories enforce ontological obedience. Items included are not only preserved but <b>(3)</b> _____, endowed with rhetorical inertia that naturalizes their interpretive authority. What remains uncatalogued is condemned to historiographic latency—neither denied nor debated, but suspended in bureaucratic limbo. Hence, archiving becomes not an act of recall, but of inscription: it encodes memory into a topology of relevance. In doing so, it <b>(4)</b> _____ affective possibility—dictating not only what can be known, but what may be mourned, commemorated, or forgotten. To critique this system is not to impugn documentation, but to unmask its metaphysical scaffolding: the unseen grammar that adjudicates between datum and debris, artifact and aberration, history and noise.The scholar’s task, then, is not simply retrieval, but ontological sabotage: to <b>(5)</b> _____ the archive’s predicate assumptions before entering its doors.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number <b>(1)</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"elaboration"},"2":{"en":"homogenous"},"3":{"en":"protocol"},"4":{"en":"pretext"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…structuring the legibility of the past through regimes of visibility and institutional (1) _____.\"</i><br>Grammar: after the adjective 'institutional' a noun is needed, parallel to 'regimes of visibility'.<br>Meaning: <b>protocol (नियम-प्रक्रिया)</b> = official rules and procedures – the archive works through institutional procedures.<br><b>Elaboration (विस्तार)</b> – does not suit 'structuring'<br><b>Homogenous (समरूप)</b> – an adjective, not a noun<br><b>Pretext (बहाना)</b> – a false reason; meaning does not fit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): protocol.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000070466","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:</b><br>The archive, far from a passive container of memory, functions as an apparatus of epistemic engineering—structuring the legibility of the past through regimes of visibility and institutional <b>(1)</b> _____. It performs not merely as custodian, but as an authorial surrogate, retrofitting historical fragments into a narratological grammar that flatters the contours of state teleology. What escapes its rubric is not lost, but rendered <b>(2)</b> _____—denied syntactic viability within the lexicon of national legitimacy. This architecture does not conceal so much as calibrate. Through procedural neutrality, the archive creates the illusion of factual autonomy, even as its categories enforce ontological obedience. Items included are not only preserved but <b>(3)</b> _____, endowed with rhetorical inertia that naturalizes their interpretive authority. What remains uncatalogued is condemned to historiographic latency—neither denied nor debated, but suspended in bureaucratic limbo. Hence, archiving becomes not an act of recall, but of inscription: it encodes memory into a topology of relevance. In doing so, it <b>(4)</b> _____ affective possibility—dictating not only what can be known, but what may be mourned, commemorated, or forgotten. To critique this system is not to impugn documentation, but to unmask its metaphysical scaffolding: the unseen grammar that adjudicates between datum and debris, artifact and aberration, history and noise.The scholar’s task, then, is not simply retrieval, but ontological sabotage: to <b>(5)</b> _____ the archive’s predicate assumptions before entering its doors.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number <b>(2)</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"anachronistic"},"2":{"en":"inarticulable"},"3":{"en":"heretical"},"4":{"en":"peripheral"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"What escapes its rubric is not lost, but rendered (2) _____—denied syntactic viability within the lexicon of national legitimacy.\"</i><br>The dash explains the blank: what is left out cannot be expressed in the archive's 'lexicon'.<br><b>Inarticulable (अव्यक्त करने योग्य नहीं)</b> = impossible to express in words ✔<br><b>Anachronistic (कालभ्रमित)</b> = belonging to another period<br><b>Heretical (विधर्मी)</b> = against accepted belief<br><b>Peripheral (सीमांत)</b> = of minor importance – does not match 'denied syntactic viability'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): inarticulable.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000070467","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:</b><br>The archive, far from a passive container of memory, functions as an apparatus of epistemic engineering—structuring the legibility of the past through regimes of visibility and institutional <b>(1)</b> _____. It performs not merely as custodian, but as an authorial surrogate, retrofitting historical fragments into a narratological grammar that flatters the contours of state teleology. What escapes its rubric is not lost, but rendered <b>(2)</b> _____—denied syntactic viability within the lexicon of national legitimacy. This architecture does not conceal so much as calibrate. Through procedural neutrality, the archive creates the illusion of factual autonomy, even as its categories enforce ontological obedience. Items included are not only preserved but <b>(3)</b> _____, endowed with rhetorical inertia that naturalizes their interpretive authority. What remains uncatalogued is condemned to historiographic latency—neither denied nor debated, but suspended in bureaucratic limbo. Hence, archiving becomes not an act of recall, but of inscription: it encodes memory into a topology of relevance. In doing so, it <b>(4)</b> _____ affective possibility—dictating not only what can be known, but what may be mourned, commemorated, or forgotten. To critique this system is not to impugn documentation, but to unmask its metaphysical scaffolding: the unseen grammar that adjudicates between datum and debris, artifact and aberration, history and noise.The scholar’s task, then, is not simply retrieval, but ontological sabotage: to <b>(5)</b> _____ the archive’s predicate assumptions before entering its doors.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number <b>(3)</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"contextualized"},"2":{"en":"indexed"},"3":{"en":"canonized"},"4":{"en":"diluted"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Items included are not only preserved but (3) _____, endowed with rhetorical inertia that naturalizes their interpretive authority.\"</i><br>The items gain authority that seems natural, so they are raised to an accepted, authoritative status.<br><b>Canonized (प्रामाणिक/मान्य घोषित)</b> = accepted as authoritative ✔<br><b>Contextualized (संदर्भित)</b> – placing in context; does not give authority<br><b>Indexed (अनुक्रमित)</b> – merely listed<br><b>Diluted (कमज़ोर किया गया)</b> – opposite of gaining authority<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): canonized.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000070468","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:</b><br>The archive, far from a passive container of memory, functions as an apparatus of epistemic engineering—structuring the legibility of the past through regimes of visibility and institutional <b>(1)</b> _____. It performs not merely as custodian, but as an authorial surrogate, retrofitting historical fragments into a narratological grammar that flatters the contours of state teleology. What escapes its rubric is not lost, but rendered <b>(2)</b> _____—denied syntactic viability within the lexicon of national legitimacy. This architecture does not conceal so much as calibrate. Through procedural neutrality, the archive creates the illusion of factual autonomy, even as its categories enforce ontological obedience. Items included are not only preserved but <b>(3)</b> _____, endowed with rhetorical inertia that naturalizes their interpretive authority. What remains uncatalogued is condemned to historiographic latency—neither denied nor debated, but suspended in bureaucratic limbo. Hence, archiving becomes not an act of recall, but of inscription: it encodes memory into a topology of relevance. In doing so, it <b>(4)</b> _____ affective possibility—dictating not only what can be known, but what may be mourned, commemorated, or forgotten. To critique this system is not to impugn documentation, but to unmask its metaphysical scaffolding: the unseen grammar that adjudicates between datum and debris, artifact and aberration, history and noise.The scholar’s task, then, is not simply retrieval, but ontological sabotage: to <b>(5)</b> _____ the archive’s predicate assumptions before entering its doors.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number <b>(4)</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"differentiate"},"2":{"en":"regulates"},"3":{"en":"fabricates"},"4":{"en":"memorializes"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"In doing so, it (4) _____ affective possibility—dictating not only what can be known, but what may be mourned, commemorated, or forgotten.\"</i><br>Grammar: singular subject 'it' needs a verb ending in '-s'.<br>Meaning: 'dictating' shows control, so <b>regulates (नियंत्रित करता है)</b> fits.<br><b>differentiate</b> – plural form with singular 'it'<br><b>fabricates (गढ़ता है)</b> – means invents falsely; not 'dictating'<br><b>memorializes (स्मृति में रखता है)</b> – only one of the listed acts, not control over all<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): regulates.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000070469","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"<b>In the given passage, some words have been deleted. Read the passage intently and choose the most appropriate option to fill in each blank:</b><br>The archive, far from a passive container of memory, functions as an apparatus of epistemic engineering—structuring the legibility of the past through regimes of visibility and institutional <b>(1)</b> _____. It performs not merely as custodian, but as an authorial surrogate, retrofitting historical fragments into a narratological grammar that flatters the contours of state teleology. What escapes its rubric is not lost, but rendered <b>(2)</b> _____—denied syntactic viability within the lexicon of national legitimacy. This architecture does not conceal so much as calibrate. Through procedural neutrality, the archive creates the illusion of factual autonomy, even as its categories enforce ontological obedience. Items included are not only preserved but <b>(3)</b> _____, endowed with rhetorical inertia that naturalizes their interpretive authority. What remains uncatalogued is condemned to historiographic latency—neither denied nor debated, but suspended in bureaucratic limbo. Hence, archiving becomes not an act of recall, but of inscription: it encodes memory into a topology of relevance. In doing so, it <b>(4)</b> _____ affective possibility—dictating not only what can be known, but what may be mourned, commemorated, or forgotten. To critique this system is not to impugn documentation, but to unmask its metaphysical scaffolding: the unseen grammar that adjudicates between datum and debris, artifact and aberration, history and noise.The scholar’s task, then, is not simply retrieval, but ontological sabotage: to <b>(5)</b> _____ the archive’s predicate assumptions before entering its doors.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number <b>(5)</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"integrate"},"2":{"en":"destabilize"},"3":{"en":"invoke"},"4":{"en":"mimic"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"The scholar’s task, then, is not simply retrieval, but ontological sabotage: to (5) _____ the archive’s predicate assumptions…\"</i><br>'Sabotage' means undermining, so the scholar must shake the archive's assumptions.<br><b>Destabilize (अस्थिर करना)</b> ✔<br><b>Integrate (एकीकृत करना)</b> – opposite of sabotage<br><b>Invoke (आह्वान करना)</b> – calling upon; supports rather than undermines<br><b>Mimic (नकल करना)</b> – copying; does not fit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): destabilize.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000070470","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the correct collocation:</b><br>His explanation was _____, and to the point. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"short and right"},"2":{"en":"quick and good"},"3":{"en":"clear and concise"},"4":{"en":"smart and simple"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'clear and concise' (स्पष्ट और संक्षिप्त) is the fixed collocation for an explanation that is easy to follow and brief.</b><br>It matches 'and to the point'.<br>Correct sentence: His explanation was <b>clear and concise</b>, and to the point.<br>short and right, quick and good, smart and simple – not standard collocations for an explanation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): clear and concise.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000070471","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>They might announce the winner tomorrow. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The winner might be announced tomorrow."},"2":{"en":"The winner may be announced tomorrow."},"3":{"en":"The winner will be announced tomorrow."},"4":{"en":"The winner might have been announced tomorrow."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Modal + V1 (active) → same modal + be + V3 (passive).</b><br>'might announce' → 'might be announced'; 'by them' is dropped.<br>Passive: The winner <b>might be announced</b> tomorrow.<br>Option 2 – modal 'might' changed to 'may'<br>Option 3 – modal changed to 'will'<br>Option 4 – 'might have been' refers to the past, not 'tomorrow'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The winner might be announced tomorrow.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000070472","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>The dog bit the postman. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The postman is bitten by the dog."},"2":{"en":"The postman was bitten by the dog."},"3":{"en":"The postman has been bitten by the dog."},"4":{"en":"The postman had been bitten by the dog."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past active (V2) → passive: was/were + V3.</b><br>'bit' → 'was bitten'; the object 'the postman' becomes the subject.<br>Passive: The postman <b>was bitten</b> by the dog.<br>Option 1 – simple present passive<br>Option 3 – present perfect passive<br>Option 4 – past perfect passive<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The postman was bitten by the dog.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000070473","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:</b><br>The passengers were confirmed to have been informed about the delay before boarding. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It was confirmed the passengers were informed before boarding."},"2":{"en":"Someone confirmed that passengers had been informed before boarding."},"3":{"en":"Officials confirmed that the passengers had been informed about the delay before boarding."},"4":{"en":"The delay was confirmed to have been known to the passengers."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'was/were confirmed to have been + V3' → active: Agent + confirmed + that + subject + had been + V3.</b><br>The confirming agent is supplied ('Officials'); the earlier action becomes past perfect.<br>Active: <b>Officials confirmed</b> that the passengers had been informed about the delay before boarding.<br>Option 1 – still passive and drops 'about the delay'<br>Option 2 – drops 'the' and 'about the delay'<br>Option 4 – changes the meaning to 'the delay was known'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Officials confirmed that the passengers had been informed about the delay before boarding.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000070474","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:</b><br>The director was informed to have his team submit the revised plan by Friday. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The team submitted the plan as the director was informed."},"2":{"en":"Someone informed the director that he must have the team submit the revised plan."},"3":{"en":"The plan was submitted by Friday, as informed."},"4":{"en":"The director was told that he should submit the team’s plan."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Passive with no agent → active with an indefinite subject ('Someone'); the infinitive instruction becomes a 'that' clause.</b><br>'was informed to have his team submit' → 'Someone informed the director that he must have the team submit…'.<br>Active: <b>Someone informed</b> the director that he must have the team submit the revised plan.<br>Option 1 – says the plan was submitted; meaning changed<br>Option 3 – still passive and changes meaning<br>Option 4 – still passive ('was told') and the director, not the team, submits<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Someone informed the director that he must have the team submit the revised plan.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000070475","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>He <b><i>has went</i></b> to the market. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"has go"},"2":{"en":"had gone"},"3":{"en":"went"},"4":{"en":"has gone"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The present perfect is has/have + V3; the V3 of 'go' is 'gone'.</b><br>'went' is V2 and cannot follow 'has'.<br>Correct sentence: He <b>has gone</b> to the market.<br>has go – V1 after 'has'<br>had gone – past perfect changes the tense<br>went – grammatical, but it changes the present perfect meaning (he is still away)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): has gone.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000070476","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence</b><br>P: and cultural pluralism Q: India’s democratic fabric R: is deeply rooted S: in historical dialogues [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRSP"},"2":{"en":"PRSQ"},"3":{"en":"QSPR"},"4":{"en":"QPSR"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br><b>Q</b> 'India's democratic fabric' is the subject and opens the sentence.<br><b>R</b> 'is deeply rooted' gives the verb.<br><b>S</b> 'in historical dialogues' completes 'rooted in…'.<br><b>P</b> 'and cultural pluralism' joins a second noun to 'historical dialogues'.<br>India's democratic fabric is deeply rooted in historical dialogues and cultural pluralism.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000070477","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"<b>A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.</b><br>She said, “John must have missed the train.” [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said John might missed the train."},"2":{"en":"She said that John must had missed the train."},"3":{"en":"She said that John must have missed the train."},"4":{"en":"She said John had to miss the train."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'must have + V3' (a deduction about the past) does not change in indirect speech.</b><br>Indirect: She said that John <b>must have missed</b> the train.<br>Option 1 – 'might missed' – a modal takes V1, and 'must' should not change<br>Option 2 – 'must had' – a modal cannot take 'had'<br>Option 4 – 'had to miss' changes deduction into obligation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): She said that John must have missed the train.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000070478","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"<b>A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.</b><br>The coach said that practice would begin at 6 a.m. the next day. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“Practice will begin at 6 a.m. tomorrow,” said the coach."},"2":{"en":"“Practice would begin at 6 a.m. the next day,” the coach said."},"3":{"en":"“We begin practice at 6 a.m.,” said the coach."},"4":{"en":"“Practice is starting at 6 a.m. tomorrow,” said the coach."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: In direct speech 'would' goes back to 'will' and 'the next day' goes back to 'tomorrow'.</b><br>Direct: “Practice <b>will begin</b> at 6 a.m. <b>tomorrow</b>,” said the coach.<br>Option 2 – keeps the reported forms 'would' and 'the next day'<br>Option 3 – drops 'tomorrow' and changes the tense<br>Option 4 – present continuous 'is starting' changes the tense<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “Practice will begin at 6 a.m. tomorrow,” said the coach.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000070479","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"<b>A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.</b><br>He said that were it not for her, they would have lost everything. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“If it was not for her, we would have lost everything,” he said."},"2":{"en":"“If not for her, we would have lost it all,” he said."},"3":{"en":"“Were it not for her, we would have lost everything,” he said."},"4":{"en":"“Had it not been for her, we would lose everything,” he said."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Conditional (subjunctive) forms do not change between direct and indirect speech; only the pronouns change.</b><br>'they' → 'we'; 'were it not for her … would have lost' stays the same.<br>Direct: “<b>Were it not for her</b>, we would have lost everything,” he said.<br>Option 1 – 'If it was not' changes the subjunctive form<br>Option 2 – changes the wording ('lost it all')<br>Option 4 – 'would lose' does not match the original<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): “Were it not for her, we would have lost everything,” he said.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000070480","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a logical passage.</b><br>1. Therefore, libraries are evolving into community learning hubs.<br>2. The role of traditional libraries is changing.<br>3. They now offer more than just books, including digital resources and workshops.<br>4. This adaptation ensures their continued relevance in the digital age. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-4-1-3"},"2":{"en":"2-1-3-4"},"3":{"en":"3-4-2-1"},"4":{"en":"2-3-4-1"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-3-4-1</b><br><b>2</b> states the topic: the role of libraries is changing.<br><b>3</b> 'They now offer…' explains how they are changing.<br><b>4</b> 'This adaptation' refers to the change in 3 and gives its benefit.<br><b>1</b> 'Therefore' draws the conclusion.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2-3-4-1.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};